var ANS={"Apr26 Q1": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.karunya.edu&quot;&gt;Visit Karunya&lt;/a&gt;<\/pre>\n<p><code>&lt;a&gt;<\/code> is the anchor tag; <code>href<\/code> holds the address and the text between the tags is what the user clicks.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q2": "<p>The <b>ID selector<\/b>: <code>#main { color: red; }<\/code> styles the element with <code>id=\"main\"<\/code>.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q3": "<p><b>alert()<\/b>, e.g. <code>alert(\"Hello\");<\/code>. (<code>confirm()<\/code> and <code>prompt()<\/code> are the other two pop-up boxes.)<\/p>", "Apr26 Q4": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">var data = $(&quot;.t1&quot;).val();<\/pre>", "Apr26 Q5": "<p><b>JSON.stringify()<\/b>, e.g. <code>JSON.stringify({name: \"Ravi\"})<\/code> gives <code>'{\"name\":\"Ravi\"}'<\/code>.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q6": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<p><b>ng-model<\/b> is <b>two-way<\/b> binding: it ties an input to a scope variable, so typing changes the variable and the variable changes the input. <b>ng-bind<\/b> is <b>one-way<\/b>: it only displays a scope value inside an element (like <code>{{ }}<\/code>).<\/p>", "Apr26 Q7": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<p><b>$valid<\/b>, <b>$invalid<\/b>, <b>$dirty<\/b>, <b>$pristine<\/b> (also $touched, $untouched).<\/p>", "Apr26 Q8": "<p><b>fs.appendFile()<\/b> (or <code>fs.appendFileSync()<\/code>): <code>fs.appendFile(\"notes.txt\", \"new line\\n\", err =&gt; {...})<\/code> adds to the end without erasing the file.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q9": "<p>The <b>http<\/b> module: <code>const http = require(\"http\"); http.createServer(...)<\/code>.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q10": "<p><b>Mongoose<\/b> is a Node.js library (ODM, Object Data Modeling) for MongoDB. It lets you define a <b>schema<\/b> and <b>model<\/b> for documents, validates data, and gives simple methods (<code>save, find, updateOne, deleteOne<\/code>) to work with the database.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q11": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;form&gt;\n  &lt;label&gt;a) Course:&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;select name=&quot;course&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;option&gt;CSE&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;option&gt;ECE&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;option&gt;EEE&lt;/option&gt;\n  &lt;/select&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n\n  &lt;label&gt;b) Date of Birth:&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;input type=&quot;date&quot; name=&quot;dob&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n\n  &lt;label&gt;c) Gender:&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; name=&quot;gender&quot; value=&quot;Male&quot;&gt; Male\n  &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; name=&quot;gender&quot; value=&quot;Female&quot;&gt; Female\n&lt;/form&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>&lt;select&gt;<\/code> with <code>&lt;option&gt;<\/code>s gives the drop-down; <code>type=\"date\"<\/code> gives a calendar; radio buttons share the same <code>name<\/code> so only one can be selected.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q12": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css&quot;&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body class=&quot;p-3&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;&gt;Primary&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot;&gt;Secondary&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-success&quot;&gt;Success&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-info&quot;&gt;Info&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-warning&quot;&gt;Warning&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Every button needs the base class <code>btn<\/code>; the second class (<code>btn-primary<\/code>, <code>btn-secondary<\/code>, …) picks the colour. Bootstrap is linked from its CDN.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q13": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;down&quot;&gt;Slide Down&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;up&quot;&gt;Slide Up&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;toggle&quot;&gt;Slide Toggle&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;display:none;background:#cde;padding:20px;margin-top:8px&quot;&gt;\n  Sliding panel\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  $(document).ready(function () {\n    $(&quot;#down&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#panel&quot;).slideDown(&quot;slow&quot;); });\n    $(&quot;#up&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#panel&quot;).slideUp(&quot;slow&quot;); });\n    $(&quot;#toggle&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#panel&quot;).slideToggle(&quot;slow&quot;); });\n  });\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>slideDown()<\/code> reveals by increasing height, <code>slideUp()<\/code> hides by decreasing it, <code>slideToggle()<\/code> switches between the two. Speed can be \"slow\", \"fast\" or milliseconds.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q14": "<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Example<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>String (double quotes only)<\/td><td><code>\"name\": \"Ravi\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Number (integer or decimal)<\/td><td><code>\"age\": 20, \"cgpa\": 8.5<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Boolean<\/td><td><code>\"active\": true<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Null<\/td><td><code>\"middleName\": null<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Object<\/td><td><code>\"address\": { \"city\": \"Coimbatore\", \"pin\": 641114 }<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Array<\/td><td><code>\"skills\": [\"HTML\", \"CSS\", \"JS\"]<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>JSON has no date, function or undefined type; dates are stored as strings.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q15": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;div ng-app=&quot;&quot; ng-init=&quot;fruits=[&#x27;Apple&#x27;,&#x27;Mango&#x27;,&#x27;Banana&#x27;,&#x27;Orange&#x27;]&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;ol&gt;\n    &lt;li ng-repeat=&quot;f in fruits&quot;&gt;{{ f }}&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>ng-init<\/code> creates the array, and <code>ng-repeat<\/code> repeats the <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code> once for each element inside the <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q16": "<ul>\n<li><b>updateOne(filter, update)<\/b>: changes the first document that matches.<\/li>\n<li><b>updateMany(filter, update)<\/b>: changes every matching document.<\/li>\n<li><b>replaceOne(filter, newDoc)<\/b>: replaces the whole document (except _id).<\/li>\n<li>Update operators: <code>$set<\/code> (set a field), <code>$inc<\/code> (add to a number), <code>$unset<\/code> (remove a field). Option <code>{ upsert: true }<\/code> inserts if nothing matches.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">db.students.updateOne({ regno: 101 }, { $set: { cgpa: 9.1 } })\ndb.students.updateMany({ dept: &quot;CSE&quot; }, { $inc: { year: 1 } })\ndb.students.replaceOne({ regno: 102 }, { regno: 102, name: &quot;Divya&quot;, dept: &quot;IT&quot; })<\/pre>", "Apr26 Q17a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; }\n    th, td { padding: 4px 12px; text-align: center; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;table&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th colspan=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Time Table&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;th rowspan=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Hours&lt;/th&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Mon&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Tue&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Wed&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Thu&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Fri&lt;/th&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Computer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Maths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Computer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Maths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Arts&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Arts&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Maths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Computer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Arts&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Maths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th colspan=&quot;5&quot;&gt;LUNCH&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Arts&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Maths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Computer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Arts&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Maths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Computer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Maths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Computer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Maths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Arts&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul>\n<li>\"Time Table\" spans all six columns: <code>colspan=\"6\"<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>\"Hours\" covers the day row and all five period rows: <code>rowspan=\"6\"<\/code>, so the rows after it have only five cells.<\/li>\n<li>\"LUNCH\" spans the five day columns: <code>colspan=\"5\"<\/code>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Apr26 Q17b": "<p class=\"log\">Same question as <b>May24 Q23b<\/b>; the answer is repeated here.<\/p><p>HTML has three kinds of list:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Ordered list<\/b> <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code>: numbered items <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code>. Attribute <code>type<\/code> = 1, A, a, I, i and <code>start<\/code> sets the first number.<\/li>\n<li><b>Unordered list<\/b> <code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code>: bulleted items; CSS <code>list-style-type<\/code> = disc, circle, square or none.<\/li>\n<li><b>Definition (description) list<\/b> <code>&lt;dl&gt;<\/code>: terms <code>&lt;dt&gt;<\/code> each followed by a description <code>&lt;dd&gt;<\/code>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h4&gt;Ordered List&lt;/h4&gt;\n  &lt;ol type=&quot;A&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;HTML&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;CSS&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;JavaScript&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ol&gt;\n\n  &lt;h4&gt;Unordered List&lt;/h4&gt;\n  &lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type: square&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Apple&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Mango&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Banana&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n\n  &lt;h4&gt;Definition List&lt;/h4&gt;\n  &lt;dl&gt;\n    &lt;dt&gt;HTML&lt;/dt&gt;\n    &lt;dd&gt;Markup language that structures a web page.&lt;/dd&gt;\n    &lt;dt&gt;CSS&lt;/dt&gt;\n    &lt;dd&gt;Style sheet language that styles the page.&lt;/dd&gt;\n  &lt;/dl&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Lists can be nested by putting a full <code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code> or <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code> inside an <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q18a": "<p>The <code>position<\/code> property, with <code>top / right / bottom / left<\/code>, decides where an element is placed.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Value<\/th><th>Placed relative to<\/th><th>In normal flow?<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>static<\/b> (default)<\/td><td>normal flow; top/left have no effect<\/td><td>yes<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>relative<\/b><\/td><td>its own normal position<\/td><td>yes, original space kept<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>absolute<\/b><\/td><td>the nearest positioned ancestor (else the page)<\/td><td>no<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>fixed<\/b><\/td><td>the browser window; stays put when scrolling<\/td><td>no<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>sticky<\/b><\/td><td>acts relative until a scroll offset is reached, then sticks like fixed<\/td><td>yes<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  .box { width: 120px; padding: 8px; color: white; margin: 6px; }\n  .static   { position: static;   background: gray; }\n  .relative { position: relative; left: 40px; background: teal; }\n  .parent   { position: relative; height: 90px; border: 2px dashed #555; }\n  .absolute { position: absolute; right: 10px; bottom: 10px; background: crimson; }\n  .fixed    { position: fixed; top: 10px; right: 10px; background: navy; }\n  .sticky   { position: sticky; top: 0; background: orange; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;box sticky&quot;&gt;sticky&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;box static&quot;&gt;static&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;box relative&quot;&gt;relative (left 40px)&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;parent&quot;&gt;\n  parent (relative)\n  &lt;div class=&quot;box absolute&quot;&gt;absolute&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;box fixed&quot;&gt;fixed&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;p style=&quot;height:300px&quot;&gt;Scroll inside the frame: fixed stays, sticky sticks at the top.&lt;/p&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "Apr26 Q18b": "<p><b>Process<\/b>: (1) put the links in an unordered list, since a menu is a list of links; (2) remove the bullets and padding; (3) make the items sit side by side (<code>float: left<\/code> or <code>display: flex<\/code>); (4) turn each link into a block with padding, colour and no underline; (5) add a <code>:hover<\/code> colour, and an <code>active<\/code> class for the current page (Contact in the picture).<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    ul {\n      list-style-type: none;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      background-color: #333;\n      width: 600px;\n    }\n    li { float: left; }\n    li a {\n      display: block;\n      color: white;\n      text-align: center;\n      padding: 14px 30px;\n      text-decoration: none;\n    }\n    li a:hover, li a.active { background-color: #777; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#home&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#news&quot;&gt;News&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#contact&quot; class=&quot;active&quot;&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#about&quot;&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#services&quot;&gt;Services&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "Apr26 Q19a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;b&gt;Calculator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  Number1: &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;n1&quot; value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  Number2: &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;n2&quot; value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  Select Operation(+,-,*,/):\n  &lt;select id=&quot;op&quot; onchange=&quot;calculate()&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;option&gt;+&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;option&gt;-&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;option&gt;*&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;option&gt;/&lt;/option&gt;\n  &lt;/select&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Result: &lt;span id=&quot;res&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    function calculate() {\n      var a = parseFloat(document.getElementById(&quot;n1&quot;).value);\n      var b = parseFloat(document.getElementById(&quot;n2&quot;).value);\n      var op = document.getElementById(&quot;op&quot;).value;\n      var r;\n      if (op == &quot;+&quot;) r = a + b;\n      else if (op == &quot;-&quot;) r = a - b;\n      else if (op == &quot;*&quot;) r = a * b;\n      else r = (b == 0) ? &quot;Cannot divide by zero&quot; : a / b;\n      document.getElementById(&quot;res&quot;).innerHTML = r;\n    }\n    calculate();\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The <code>onchange<\/code> event on the drop-down calls <code>calculate()<\/code> every time a different operator is chosen, so the result updates immediately. <code>parseFloat<\/code> converts the text inputs to numbers (otherwise + would join them as strings: \"3\"+\"2\" = \"32\").<\/p>", "Apr26 Q19b": "<p class=\"log\">Same question as <b>May24 Q19a<\/b>; the answer is repeated here.<\/p><p>The <b>DOM<\/b> (Document Object Model) represents the page as a tree of objects; JavaScript uses the <code>document<\/code> object to find elements and change them.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>Returns<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.getElementById(\"id\")<\/code><\/td><td>the single element with that id<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.getElementsByClassName(\"c\")<\/code><\/td><td>a collection of elements with that class<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.getElementsByTagName(\"p\")<\/code><\/td><td>a collection of all elements with that tag<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.getElementsByName(\"n\")<\/code><\/td><td>elements with that name attribute (radio groups)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.querySelector(\"css\")<\/code><\/td><td>the first element matching a CSS selector<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.querySelectorAll(\"css\")<\/code><\/td><td>all elements matching a CSS selector<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>After finding an element: <code>innerHTML<\/code> / <code>innerText<\/code> change its content, <code>.style.color<\/code> its style, <code>.value<\/code> a form field's value, <code>setAttribute()<\/code> an attribute.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;h3 id=&quot;head&quot;&gt;Heading&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;info&quot;&gt;Para 1&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;info&quot;&gt;Para 2&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;city&quot; value=&quot;Coimbatore&quot;&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;One&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Two&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;button onclick=&quot;run()&quot;&gt;Run DOM methods&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  function run() {\n    document.getElementById(&quot;head&quot;).innerHTML = &quot;Changed by getElementById&quot;;\n    var infos = document.getElementsByClassName(&quot;info&quot;);\n    for (var i = 0; i &lt; infos.length; i++) infos[i].style.color = &quot;blue&quot;;\n    document.getElementsByTagName(&quot;li&quot;)[0].innerText = &quot;Changed by getElementsByTagName&quot;;\n    alert(&quot;City: &quot; + document.getElementsByName(&quot;city&quot;)[0].value);\n    document.querySelector(&quot;ul&quot;).style.border = &quot;1px solid red&quot;;\n    document.querySelectorAll(&quot;li&quot;).forEach(function (li) { li.style.fontWeight = &quot;bold&quot;; });\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "Apr26 Q20a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;add&quot;&gt;Add Textbox&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;remove&quot;&gt;Remove Textbox&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;div id=&quot;boxes&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    $(document).ready(function () {\n      $(&quot;#add&quot;).click(function () {\n        $(&quot;#boxes&quot;).append(&#x27;&lt;p class=&quot;field&quot;&gt;Enter Data: &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#x27;);\n      });\n      $(&quot;#remove&quot;).click(function () {\n        $(&quot;#boxes .field&quot;).last().remove();\n      });\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>append()<\/code> adds a new paragraph holding a label and text box at the end of the <code>#boxes<\/code> div. <code>.last().remove()<\/code> deletes the most recently added one; if none are left, nothing happens.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q20b": "<p class=\"log\">Same question as <b>May24 Q23a<\/b>; the answer is repeated here.<\/p><div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;#box { width: 120px; height: 60px; background: teal; color: white; padding: 8px; position: relative; margin-top: 10px; }&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;hide&quot;&gt;hide&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;show&quot;&gt;show&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;toggle&quot;&gt;toggle&lt;/button&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;fin&quot;&gt;fadeIn&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;fout&quot;&gt;fadeOut&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;fto&quot;&gt;fadeTo 0.3&lt;/button&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;sup&quot;&gt;slideUp&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;sdown&quot;&gt;slideDown&lt;/button&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;anim&quot;&gt;animate&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;div id=&quot;box&quot;&gt;Box&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    $(function () {\n      $(&quot;#hide&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).hide(500); });\n      $(&quot;#show&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).show(500); });\n      $(&quot;#toggle&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).toggle(); });\n      $(&quot;#fin&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).fadeIn(); });\n      $(&quot;#fout&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).fadeOut(); });\n      $(&quot;#fto&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).fadeTo(&quot;slow&quot;, 0.3); });\n      $(&quot;#sup&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).slideUp(); });\n      $(&quot;#sdown&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).slideDown(); });\n      $(&quot;#anim&quot;).click(function () {\n        $(&quot;#box&quot;).animate({ left: &quot;200px&quot;, width: &quot;180px&quot;, opacity: 0.6 }, 1000)\n                 .animate({ left: &quot;0px&quot;, width: &quot;120px&quot;, opacity: 1 }, 1000);\n      });\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Group<\/th><th>Methods<\/th><th>What happens<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Hide / show<\/td><td><code>hide(), show(), toggle()<\/code><\/td><td>change display; with a speed they shrink/grow<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Fading<\/td><td><code>fadeIn(), fadeOut(), fadeToggle(), fadeTo(speed, opacity)<\/code><\/td><td>change opacity gradually; fadeTo stops at a given opacity<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Sliding<\/td><td><code>slideDown(), slideUp(), slideToggle()<\/code><\/td><td>change height gradually<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Animation<\/td><td><code>animate({css}, speed)<\/code>, <code>stop()<\/code><\/td><td>animates any numeric CSS property; calls can be chained into a queue<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>All accept an optional speed (<code>\"slow\"<\/code>, <code>\"fast\"<\/code> or ms) and a callback that runs when the effect ends.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q21a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; padding: 4px 10px; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h3&gt;Accounts with balance above Rs.10000&lt;/h3&gt;\n  &lt;table id=&quot;tbl&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Account Name&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Account No.&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Balance&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Phone No.&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Location&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    // JSON text (as it would arrive from a server or file)\n    var text = &#x27;[&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&quot;accno&quot;:&quot;56738992334&quot;,&quot;balance&quot;:5000,&quot;phone&quot;:&quot;9842146789&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;Chennai&quot;},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Mary&quot;,&quot;accno&quot;:&quot;56738992336&quot;,&quot;balance&quot;:10000,&quot;phone&quot;:&quot;9842146779&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;Mumbai&quot;},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Shiny&quot;,&quot;accno&quot;:&quot;56738992337&quot;,&quot;balance&quot;:35000,&quot;phone&quot;:&quot;9842146569&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;Chennai&quot;},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Sarah&quot;,&quot;accno&quot;:&quot;56738992338&quot;,&quot;balance&quot;:12000,&quot;phone&quot;:&quot;9941146789&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;Hydrabad&quot;},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jones&quot;,&quot;accno&quot;:&quot;56738992339&quot;,&quot;balance&quot;:75000,&quot;phone&quot;:&quot;8842146789&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;Delhi&quot;}&#x27; +\n    &#x27;]&#x27;;\n\n    var accounts = JSON.parse(text);   // JSON string -&gt; JavaScript array of objects\n\n    for (var i = 0; i &lt; accounts.length; i++) {\n      var a = accounts[i];\n      if (a.balance &gt; 10000) {\n        document.getElementById(&quot;tbl&quot;).innerHTML +=\n          &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + a.name + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + a.accno + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + a.balance +\n          &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + a.phone + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + a.location + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&quot;;\n      }\n    }\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>JSON.parse()<\/code> turns the text into an array of objects; each value is read with dot notation (<code>a.balance<\/code>, <code>a.name<\/code>). Only Shiny, Sarah and Jones are shown: Mary's 10000 is not <i>greater<\/i> than 10000. Account and phone numbers are kept as strings because they are identifiers, not amounts.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q21b": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<p>AngularJS checks each field automatically and gives it state flags. With <code>novalidate<\/code> on the form (to switch off the browser's own pop-ups), the flags <code>myForm.field.$error.required<\/code> and <code>$error.email<\/code> show the matching message with <code>ng-show<\/code>. <code>$touched<\/code> waits until the user has left the field.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;.err { color: red; font-size: 13px; }&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div ng-app=&quot;&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;form name=&quot;myForm&quot; novalidate&gt;\n    Name:&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;uname&quot; ng-model=&quot;uname&quot; required&gt;\n    &lt;span class=&quot;err&quot; ng-show=&quot;myForm.uname.$touched &amp;&amp; myForm.uname.$error.required&quot;&gt;Name is required.&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    Email:&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;email&quot; name=&quot;email&quot; ng-model=&quot;email&quot; required&gt;\n    &lt;span class=&quot;err&quot; ng-show=&quot;myForm.email.$touched &amp;&amp; myForm.email.$error.required&quot;&gt;Email is required.&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;span class=&quot;err&quot; ng-show=&quot;myForm.email.$error.email&quot;&gt;Enter a valid email address.&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;button ng-disabled=&quot;myForm.$invalid&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Form valid: {{ myForm.$valid }}&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul><li><b>required<\/b>: <code>$error.required<\/code> is true while the field is empty.<\/li>\n<li><b>type=\"email\"<\/b>: <code>$error.email<\/code> is true when the text is not in name@domain form.<\/li>\n<li><code>ng-disabled=\"myForm.$invalid\"<\/code> keeps Submit disabled until every rule passes.<\/li><\/ul>", "Apr26 Q22a": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body ng-app=&quot;emiApp&quot; ng-controller=&quot;emiCtrl&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;b&gt;Loan EMI Calculator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  Loan Amount(Rs): &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; ng-model=&quot;p&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  Annual Interest(%): &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; ng-model=&quot;rate&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  Tenure(Months): &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; ng-model=&quot;n&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;button ng-click=&quot;calculate()&quot;&gt;Calculate EMI&lt;/button&gt;\n\n  &lt;div ng-show=&quot;emi&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;EMI: Rs.{{ emi }} per month&lt;br&gt;\n    Total Repayment: Rs.{{ total }}&lt;br&gt;\n    Total Interest: Rs.{{ interest }}&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    angular.module(&quot;emiApp&quot;, []).controller(&quot;emiCtrl&quot;, function ($scope) {\n      $scope.p = 100000; $scope.rate = 10.99; $scope.n = 12;\n      $scope.calculate = function () {\n        var r = $scope.rate / 12 / 100;               // monthly rate\n        var x = Math.pow(1 + r, $scope.n);\n        $scope.emi = Math.round($scope.p * r * x / (x - 1));   // E = p*r*(1+r)^n / ((1+r)^n - 1)\n        $scope.total = $scope.emi * $scope.n;\n        $scope.interest = $scope.total - $scope.p;\n      };\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The inputs are bound to scope variables with <code>ng-model<\/code>. <code>ng-click<\/code> runs <code>calculate()<\/code>, which converts the yearly rate to a monthly rate r and applies the formula. The EMI is rounded to whole rupees (as in the paper's sample); total repayment = EMI × n and total interest = total − principal. With the paper's input (Rs.100000, 10.99%, 12 months) it gives exactly the sample: EMI Rs.8838, total Rs.106056, interest Rs.6056.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q22b": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<p><b>Routing<\/b> makes a single-page application (SPA): the page loads once, and only the part inside <code>ng-view<\/code> is swapped when a link is clicked. It needs the <b>ngRoute<\/b> module (<code>angular-route.js<\/code>), which is added as a dependency. <code>$routeProvider.when(path, {template or templateUrl})<\/code> maps each URL path to a view, and <code>otherwise()<\/code> is the default. Links use <code>#!/path<\/code>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular-route.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body ng-app=&quot;myApp&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Home Page&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!login&quot;&gt;Login&lt;/a&gt; |\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!signup&quot;&gt;New User Sign Up&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;hr&gt;\n  &lt;div ng-view&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    var app = angular.module(&quot;myApp&quot;, [&quot;ngRoute&quot;]);\n    app.config(function ($routeProvider) {\n      $routeProvider\n        .when(&quot;/login&quot;, {\n          template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;Login&lt;/h3&gt;Username: &lt;input&gt;&lt;br&gt;Password: &lt;input type=&#x27;password&#x27;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;button&gt;Login&lt;/button&gt;&quot;\n        })\n        .when(&quot;/signup&quot;, {\n          template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;New User Sign Up&lt;/h3&gt;Name: &lt;input&gt;&lt;br&gt;Email: &lt;input type=&#x27;email&#x27;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;button&gt;Sign Up&lt;/button&gt;&quot;\n        })\n        .otherwise({\n          template: &quot;&lt;p&gt;Welcome! Choose Login or Sign Up above.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;\n        });\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>In a real project each view is usually its own file, given with <code>templateUrl: \"login.html\"<\/code>.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q23": "<p>Express serves the form on <code>/<\/code> and receives it on <code>/server<\/code>; Mongoose saves it to the <code>users<\/code> collection of the <code>company<\/code> database. Setup: <code>npm install express mongoose<\/code>, start MongoDB, run <code>node app.js<\/code>.<\/p>\n<p><b>index.html<\/b><\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h3&gt;New User Registration&lt;/h3&gt;\n  &lt;form action=&quot;/server&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;\n    Name: &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;name&quot; required&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    Email: &lt;input type=&quot;email&quot; name=&quot;email&quot; required&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    Phone: &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;phone&quot; required&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    State:\n    &lt;select name=&quot;state&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;option&gt;Kerala&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;option&gt;Tamil Nadu&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;option&gt;Karnataka&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;/select&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Register&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre>\n<p><b>app.js<\/b><\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const express = require(&quot;express&quot;);\nconst mongoose = require(&quot;mongoose&quot;);\nconst path = require(&quot;path&quot;);\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));   // read form data\n\nmongoose.connect(&quot;mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/company&quot;)\n  .then(() =&gt; console.log(&quot;Connected to MongoDB&quot;))\n  .catch((err) =&gt; console.log(err.message));\n\nconst userSchema = new mongoose.Schema({\n  name: String, email: String, phone: String, state: String\n});\nconst User = mongoose.model(&quot;User&quot;, userSchema, &quot;users&quot;);   // collection &quot;users&quot;\n\napp.get(&quot;/&quot;, (req, res) =&gt; {\n  res.sendFile(path.join(__dirname, &quot;index.html&quot;));\n});\n\napp.post(&quot;/server&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; {\n  try {\n    await new User(req.body).save();\n    res.send(&quot;&lt;b&gt;Data Saved in MongoDB Database Successfully&lt;/b&gt;&quot;);\n  } catch (err) {\n    res.status(500).send(&quot;Error saving data: &quot; + err.message);\n  }\n});\n\napp.listen(2000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;Server running at http://localhost:2000/&quot;));<\/pre>\n<p><b>Run<\/b> (the form submitted with curl, then the database checked in mongosh):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">$ node app.js\nServer running at http://localhost:2000/\nConnected to MongoDB\n\n$ curl -X POST http://localhost:2000/server -d &quot;name=Ananya&amp;email=ananya@gmail.com&amp;phone=9876543210&amp;state=Kerala&quot;\n&lt;b&gt;Data Saved in MongoDB Database Successfully&lt;/b&gt;\n\n$ mongosh company --eval &quot;db.users.find()&quot;\n[\n  {\n    _id: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022ba3f90ecd629a9b88a8&#x27;),\n    name: &#x27;Ananya&#x27;,\n    email: &#x27;ananya@gmail.com&#x27;,\n    phone: &#x27;9876543210&#x27;,\n    state: &#x27;Kerala&#x27;,\n    __v: 0\n  }\n]<\/pre>\n<p><code>express.urlencoded()<\/code> parses the POSTed form into <code>req.body<\/code>, whose keys are the inputs' <code>name<\/code> attributes. The third argument to <code>mongoose.model<\/code> fixes the collection name to <code>users<\/code>.<\/p>", "Apr26 Q24": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">// i) database\nuse bank\n\n// ii) collection\ndb.createCollection(&quot;account&quot;)\n\n// iii) four customers\ndb.account.insertMany([\n  { name: &quot;John&quot;, email: &quot;john@gmail.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9842146789&quot;, accno: 1001, balance: 5000 },\n  { name: &quot;Mary&quot;, email: &quot;mary@gmail.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9842146779&quot;, accno: 1002, balance: 10000 },\n  { name: &quot;Shiny&quot;, email: &quot;shiny@gmail.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9842146569&quot;, accno: 1003, balance: 35000 },\n  { name: &quot;Sarah&quot;, email: &quot;sarah@gmail.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9941146789&quot;, accno: 1004, balance: 12000 }\n])\n\n// iv) balance of one account\ndb.account.find({ accno: 1002 }, { name: 1, balance: 1, _id: 0 })\n\n// v) deposit 2000 into 1002\ndb.account.updateOne({ accno: 1002 }, { $inc: { balance: 2000 } })\n\n// vi) withdraw 3000 from 1003, only if the balance is enough\ndb.account.updateOne({ accno: 1003, balance: { $gte: 3000 } }, { $inc: { balance: -3000 } })\n\n// vii) all accounts\ndb.account.find({}, { _id: 0 })<\/pre>\n<p><b>Output<\/b> (run in mongosh):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">test&gt; use bank\nswitched to db bank\n\nbank&gt; db.createCollection(&quot;account&quot;)\n{ ok: 1 }\n\nbank&gt; db.account.insertMany([\n...   { name: &quot;John&quot;, email: &quot;john@gmail.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9842146789&quot;, accno: 1001, balance: 5000 },\n...   { name: &quot;Mary&quot;, email: &quot;mary@gmail.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9842146779&quot;, accno: 1002, balance: 10000 },\n...   { name: &quot;Shiny&quot;, email: &quot;shiny@gmail.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9842146569&quot;, accno: 1003, balance: 35000 },\n...   { name: &quot;Sarah&quot;, email: &quot;sarah@gmail.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9941146789&quot;, accno: 1004, balance: 12000 }\n... ])\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedIds: {\n    &#x27;0&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b77eec7a1553ba13d0f&#x27;),\n    &#x27;1&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b77eec7a1553ba13d10&#x27;),\n    &#x27;2&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b77eec7a1553ba13d11&#x27;),\n    &#x27;3&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b77eec7a1553ba13d12&#x27;)\n  }\n}\n\nbank&gt; db.account.find({ accno: 1002 }, { name: 1, balance: 1, _id: 0 })\n[ { name: &#x27;Mary&#x27;, balance: 10000 } ]\n\nbank&gt; db.account.updateOne({ accno: 1002 }, { $inc: { balance: 2000 } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 1,\n  modifiedCount: 1,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nbank&gt; db.account.updateOne({ accno: 1003, balance: { $gte: 3000 } }, { $inc: { balance: -3000 } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 1,\n  modifiedCount: 1,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nbank&gt; db.account.find({}, { _id: 0 })\n[\n  {\n    name: &#x27;John&#x27;,\n    email: &#x27;john@gmail.com&#x27;,\n    phone: &#x27;9842146789&#x27;,\n    accno: 1001,\n    balance: 5000\n  },\n  {\n    name: &#x27;Mary&#x27;,\n    email: &#x27;mary@gmail.com&#x27;,\n    phone: &#x27;9842146779&#x27;,\n    accno: 1002,\n    balance: 12000\n  },\n  {\n    name: &#x27;Shiny&#x27;,\n    email: &#x27;shiny@gmail.com&#x27;,\n    phone: &#x27;9842146569&#x27;,\n    accno: 1003,\n    balance: 32000\n  },\n  {\n    name: &#x27;Sarah&#x27;,\n    email: &#x27;sarah@gmail.com&#x27;,\n    phone: &#x27;9941146789&#x27;,\n    accno: 1004,\n    balance: 12000\n  }\n]<\/pre>\n<ul><li><b>$inc<\/b> adds to a number: a positive value deposits, a negative value withdraws.<\/li>\n<li>The withdrawal filter <code>balance: { $gte: 3000 }<\/code> stops the balance going negative: if it is too low nothing matches and <code>modifiedCount<\/code> is 0.<\/li>\n<li>The projection <code>{ name: 1, balance: 1, _id: 0 }<\/code> shows just the name and balance.<\/li><\/ul>", "May24 Q1": "<p class=\"log\">Same question as <b>Apr26 Q1<\/b>; the answer is repeated here.<\/p><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.karunya.edu&quot;&gt;Visit Karunya&lt;/a&gt;<\/pre>\n<p><code>&lt;a&gt;<\/code> is the anchor tag; <code>href<\/code> holds the address and the text between the tags is what the user clicks.<\/p>", "May24 Q2": "<p><b>padding<\/b>, e.g. <code>padding: 10px;<\/code> (margin is the space outside the border).<\/p>", "May24 Q3": "<p>The <b>onclick<\/b> event: <code>&lt;button onclick=\"show()\"&gt;Click&lt;/button&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "May24 Q4": "<p><b>fadeToggle()<\/b>: <code>$(\"#box\").fadeToggle();<\/code> fades in if hidden, fades out if visible.<\/p>", "May24 Q5": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">var emp = { &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Ravi&quot;, &quot;age&quot;: 30, &quot;designation&quot;: &quot;Manager&quot; };<\/pre>", "May24 Q6": "<p><b>JSON.parse()<\/b>: <code>var obj = JSON.parse('{\"name\":\"Ravi\"}');<\/code><\/p>", "May24 Q7": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<p><b>$pristine<\/b> is true while the user has <b>not yet changed<\/b> the field; <b>$dirty<\/b> becomes true once the user <b>has changed<\/b> it. They are opposites.<\/p>", "May24 Q8": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div ng-app=&quot;&quot; ng-init=&quot;num=10&quot;&gt;{{ num }}&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre>\n<p>(or <code>&lt;div ng-init=\"num=10\" ng-bind=\"num\"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<\/code>). It displays 10.<\/p>", "May24 Q9": "<p class=\"log\">Same question as <b>Apr26 Q9<\/b>; the answer is repeated here.<\/p><p>The <b>http<\/b> module: <code>const http = require(\"http\"); http.createServer(...)<\/code>.<\/p>", "May24 Q10": "<p><b>db.createCollection()<\/b>: <code>db.createCollection(\"employee\")<\/code>.<\/p>", "May24 Q11": "<ul>\n<li><b>&lt;audio&gt;<\/b> plays sound: <code>&lt;audio src=\"song.mp3\" controls&gt;&lt;/audio&gt;<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>&lt;video&gt;<\/b> plays video: <code>&lt;video src=\"movie.mp4\" width=\"320\" controls autoplay muted&gt;&lt;/video&gt;<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>&lt;iframe&gt;<\/b> embeds another page, a YouTube video or a Google Map: <code>&lt;iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/VIDEO_ID\" width=\"400\" height=\"250\"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;<\/code><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><code>controls<\/code> shows play/pause/volume; <code>&lt;source&gt;<\/code> tags inside audio/video can give several formats for different browsers.<\/p>", "May24 Q12": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  div {\n    width: 200px;\n    padding: 20px;\n    background-color: lightblue;\n    color: black;\n  }\n  div:hover {\n    background-color: navy;\n    color: white;\n  }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;Move the cursor over me&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The <code>:hover<\/code> pseudo-class applies only while the mouse is over the div.<\/p>", "May24 Q13": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;button onclick=&quot;alert(&#x27;This is an alert box&#x27;)&quot;&gt;Alert&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button onclick=&quot;ask()&quot;&gt;Confirm&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button onclick=&quot;askName()&quot;&gt;Prompt&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;p id=&quot;out&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  function ask() {\n    var ok = confirm(&quot;Do you want to continue?&quot;);\n    document.getElementById(&quot;out&quot;).innerHTML = ok ? &quot;You pressed OK&quot; : &quot;You pressed Cancel&quot;;\n  }\n  function askName() {\n    var name = prompt(&quot;Enter your name:&quot;, &quot;&quot;);\n    document.getElementById(&quot;out&quot;).innerHTML = &quot;Hello &quot; + name;\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul><li><b>alert()<\/b>: shows a message with an OK button; returns nothing.<\/li>\n<li><b>confirm()<\/b>: OK / Cancel; returns <code>true<\/code> or <code>false<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><b>prompt()<\/b>: asks for input; returns the text typed (or <code>null<\/code> on Cancel).<\/li><\/ul>", "May24 Q14": "<p class=\"log\">Same question as <b>Apr26 Q14<\/b>; the answer is repeated here.<\/p><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Example<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>String (double quotes only)<\/td><td><code>\"name\": \"Ravi\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Number (integer or decimal)<\/td><td><code>\"age\": 20, \"cgpa\": 8.5<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Boolean<\/td><td><code>\"active\": true<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Null<\/td><td><code>\"middleName\": null<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Object<\/td><td><code>\"address\": { \"city\": \"Coimbatore\", \"pin\": 641114 }<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Array<\/td><td><code>\"skills\": [\"HTML\", \"CSS\", \"JS\"]<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>JSON has no date, function or undefined type; dates are stored as strings.<\/p>", "May24 Q15": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;div ng-app=&quot;&quot; ng-init=&quot;d=&#x27;2023-04-12&#x27;; price=1000; name=&#x27;alice&#x27;&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;a) Date: {{ d | date:&#x27;dd/MM/yyyy&#x27; }}&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;b) Price: {{ price | currency:&#x27;₹&#x27; }}&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;c) Name: {{ name | uppercase }}&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Filters are applied with the pipe <code>|<\/code>: <code>date<\/code> formats a date, <code>currency<\/code> adds the symbol and thousands separator, <code>uppercase<\/code> capitalises. (currency also shows .00; <code>currency:'₹':0<\/code> hides the decimals.)<\/p>", "May24 Q16": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const fs = require(&quot;fs&quot;);\n\nfs.readFile(&quot;data.txt&quot;, &quot;utf8&quot;, (err, data) =&gt; {\n  if (err) {\n    console.log(&quot;Error: &quot; + err.message);\n    return;\n  }\n  console.log(data);\n});<\/pre>\n<p><b>Output<\/b> (data.txt holds two lines):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">$ node read.js\nWelcome to Node.js\nThis file was read with fs.readFile<\/pre>\n<p><code>readFile<\/code> is asynchronous: Node continues and calls the callback with the contents when reading finishes. <code>\"utf8\"<\/code> returns text instead of a raw Buffer.<\/p>", "May24 Q17": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    form { width: 340px; border: 1px solid black; padding: 0 8px 8px; font-family: serif; }\n    .req { color: darkred; }\n    p { margin: 14px 0; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;form action=&quot;#&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Survey Form&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;hr&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;First name:&lt;span class=&quot;req&quot;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;fname&quot; placeholder=&quot;first name&quot; required&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Last name:&lt;span class=&quot;req&quot;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;lname&quot; placeholder=&quot;last name&quot; required&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Date:&lt;span class=&quot;req&quot;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;date&quot; name=&quot;date&quot; required&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Email:&lt;span class=&quot;req&quot;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;email&quot; name=&quot;email&quot; placeholder=&quot;xxxx@gmail.com&quot; required&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Mobile&lt;span class=&quot;req&quot;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;tel&quot; name=&quot;mobile&quot; placeholder=&quot;9988776655&quot; pattern=&quot;[0-9]{10}&quot;\n             title=&quot;Enter a 10-digit mobile number&quot; required&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Gender:&lt;span class=&quot;req&quot;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; name=&quot;gender&quot; value=&quot;Male&quot; required&gt; Male\n      &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; name=&quot;gender&quot; value=&quot;Female&quot;&gt; Female&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Age:&lt;span class=&quot;req&quot;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; name=&quot;age&quot; placeholder=&quot;18-25&quot; min=&quot;18&quot; max=&quot;25&quot; required&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Which game you like?&lt;span class=&quot;req&quot;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; name=&quot;game&quot; value=&quot;League of Legends&quot;&gt; League of Legends&lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; name=&quot;game&quot; value=&quot;CrossFire&quot;&gt; CrossFire&lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; name=&quot;game&quot; value=&quot;Fortnite Battle Royale&quot;&gt; Fortnite Battle Royale&lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; name=&quot;game&quot; value=&quot;Minecraft&quot;&gt; Minecraft&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;hr&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Submit&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Requirement<\/th><th>Attribute used<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>All fields mandatory<\/td><td><code>required<\/code> on every input (on one radio of a group is enough)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Placeholders<\/td><td><code>placeholder=\"first name\"<\/code> etc., as in the picture<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Age 18 to 25<\/td><td><code>type=\"number\" min=\"18\" max=\"25\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>10-digit mobile<\/td><td><code>pattern=\"[0-9]{10}\"<\/code>; <code>title<\/code> gives the message shown<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Email format<\/td><td><code>type=\"email\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>HTML cannot make \"at least one checkbox\" required on its own; that needs a few lines of JavaScript (check that one of them is <code>checked<\/code> on submit).<\/p>", "May24 Q18a": "<p class=\"log\">Same question as <b>Apr26 Q18b<\/b>; the answer is repeated here.<\/p><p><b>Process<\/b>: (1) put the links in an unordered list, since a menu is a list of links; (2) remove the bullets and padding; (3) make the items sit side by side (<code>float: left<\/code> or <code>display: flex<\/code>); (4) turn each link into a block with padding, colour and no underline; (5) add a <code>:hover<\/code> colour, and an <code>active<\/code> class for the current page (Contact in the picture).<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    ul {\n      list-style-type: none;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      background-color: #333;\n      width: 600px;\n    }\n    li { float: left; }\n    li a {\n      display: block;\n      color: white;\n      text-align: center;\n      padding: 14px 30px;\n      text-decoration: none;\n    }\n    li a:hover, li a.active { background-color: #777; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#home&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#news&quot;&gt;News&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#contact&quot; class=&quot;active&quot;&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#about&quot;&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#services&quot;&gt;Services&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "May24 Q18b": "<p>A <b>selector<\/b> picks which elements a CSS rule applies to.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  * { font-family: Arial; }                 /* 1. universal: every element */\n  p { color: navy; }                        /* 2. element (type): all &lt;p&gt; */\n  #title { font-size: 22px; }               /* 3. id: the one element with id=&quot;title&quot; */\n  .note { background: lightyellow; }        /* 4. class: every element with class=&quot;note&quot; */\n  h3, h4 { color: green; }                  /* 5. group: several selectors, one rule */\n  div p { font-style: italic; }             /* 6. descendant: &lt;p&gt; anywhere inside a &lt;div&gt; */\n  a:hover { color: red; }                   /* 7. pseudo-class: a state */\n  input[type=&quot;text&quot;] { border: 2px solid orange; }   /* 8. attribute */\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;p id=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Id selector&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Class selector&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Grouped h3&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Grouped h4&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Descendant: p inside div&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Hover me&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; value=&quot;attribute selector&quot;&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Selector<\/th><th>Syntax<\/th><th>Selects<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Universal<\/td><td><code>*<\/code><\/td><td>all elements<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Element<\/td><td><code>p<\/code><\/td><td>all elements of that tag<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>ID<\/td><td><code>#title<\/code><\/td><td>the element with that id (unique)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Class<\/td><td><code>.note<\/code><\/td><td>all elements with that class<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Grouping<\/td><td><code>h3, h4<\/code><\/td><td>each listed selector<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Descendant<\/td><td><code>div p<\/code><\/td><td>p inside div at any depth (<code>div &gt; p<\/code> = direct child only)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Pseudo-class<\/td><td><code>a:hover<\/code><\/td><td>an element in a state (hover, first-child, visited)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Attribute<\/td><td><code>input[type=\"text\"]<\/code><\/td><td>elements with that attribute value<\/td><\/tr><\/table>", "May24 Q19a": "<p>The <b>DOM<\/b> (Document Object Model) represents the page as a tree of objects; JavaScript uses the <code>document<\/code> object to find elements and change them.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>Returns<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.getElementById(\"id\")<\/code><\/td><td>the single element with that id<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.getElementsByClassName(\"c\")<\/code><\/td><td>a collection of elements with that class<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.getElementsByTagName(\"p\")<\/code><\/td><td>a collection of all elements with that tag<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.getElementsByName(\"n\")<\/code><\/td><td>elements with that name attribute (radio groups)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.querySelector(\"css\")<\/code><\/td><td>the first element matching a CSS selector<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.querySelectorAll(\"css\")<\/code><\/td><td>all elements matching a CSS selector<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>After finding an element: <code>innerHTML<\/code> / <code>innerText<\/code> change its content, <code>.style.color<\/code> its style, <code>.value<\/code> a form field's value, <code>setAttribute()<\/code> an attribute.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;h3 id=&quot;head&quot;&gt;Heading&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;info&quot;&gt;Para 1&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;info&quot;&gt;Para 2&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;city&quot; value=&quot;Coimbatore&quot;&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;One&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Two&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;button onclick=&quot;run()&quot;&gt;Run DOM methods&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  function run() {\n    document.getElementById(&quot;head&quot;).innerHTML = &quot;Changed by getElementById&quot;;\n    var infos = document.getElementsByClassName(&quot;info&quot;);\n    for (var i = 0; i &lt; infos.length; i++) infos[i].style.color = &quot;blue&quot;;\n    document.getElementsByTagName(&quot;li&quot;)[0].innerText = &quot;Changed by getElementsByTagName&quot;;\n    alert(&quot;City: &quot; + document.getElementsByName(&quot;city&quot;)[0].value);\n    document.querySelector(&quot;ul&quot;).style.border = &quot;1px solid red&quot;;\n    document.querySelectorAll(&quot;li&quot;).forEach(function (li) { li.style.fontWeight = &quot;bold&quot;; });\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "May24 Q19b": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; padding: 4px 12px; text-align: center; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;table id=&quot;emp&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;name&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;empid&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;gender&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;location&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;salary&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    var json = &#x27;{ &quot;employees&quot;: [&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;David&quot;,&quot;empid&quot;:897,&quot;gender&quot;:&quot;male&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;chennai&quot;,&quot;salary&quot;:20000},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Vimal&quot;,&quot;empid&quot;:682,&quot;gender&quot;:&quot;male&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;coimbatore&quot;,&quot;salary&quot;:35000},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Raj&quot;,&quot;empid&quot;:901,&quot;gender&quot;:&quot;male&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;bangalore&quot;,&quot;salary&quot;:40000},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Lee&quot;,&quot;empid&quot;:354,&quot;gender&quot;:&quot;female&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;hyderbad&quot;,&quot;salary&quot;:30000},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tia&quot;,&quot;empid&quot;:789,&quot;gender&quot;:&quot;female&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:&quot;kolkata&quot;,&quot;salary&quot;:15000}&#x27; +\n    &#x27;] }&#x27;;\n\n    var obj = JSON.parse(json);          // JSON text -&gt; JavaScript object\n    var rows = &quot;&quot;;\n    obj.employees.forEach(function (e) {\n      rows += &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + e.name + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + e.empid + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + e.gender +\n              &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + e.location + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + e.salary + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&quot;;\n    });\n    document.getElementById(&quot;emp&quot;).innerHTML += rows;\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The JSON object holds an array <code>employees<\/code> of five objects. <code>JSON.parse()<\/code> converts it; <code>forEach<\/code> walks the array and builds one table row per employee, added to the table with <code>innerHTML<\/code>.<\/p>", "May24 Q20a": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular-route.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body ng-app=&quot;spa&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Student Profile&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!personal&quot;&gt;Personal Details&lt;/a&gt; |\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!academic&quot;&gt;Academic Details&lt;/a&gt; |\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!internship&quot;&gt;Internship Details&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;hr&gt;\n  &lt;div ng-view&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    angular.module(&quot;spa&quot;, [&quot;ngRoute&quot;]).config(function ($routeProvider) {\n      $routeProvider\n        .when(&quot;/personal&quot;,   { template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;Personal Details&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Name: Ananya R&lt;br&gt;DOB: 12-05-2006&lt;br&gt;City: Coimbatore&lt;/p&gt;&quot; })\n        .when(&quot;/academic&quot;,   { template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;Academic Details&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;B.Tech CSE, CGPA 8.7&lt;/p&gt;&quot; })\n        .when(&quot;/internship&quot;, { template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;Internship Details&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Web Developer Intern, 2 months&lt;/p&gt;&quot; })\n        .otherwise({ redirectTo: &quot;/personal&quot; });\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The <b>ngRoute<\/b> module maps each <code>#!/path<\/code> to a view; only the <code>ng-view<\/code> div changes when a link is clicked, so the page never reloads. In a real project each view would be a separate file given with <code>templateUrl<\/code>.<\/p>", "May24 Q20b": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Directive<\/th><th>Purpose<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>ng-app<\/td><td>marks the root of the AngularJS application; Angular starts here<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>ng-model<\/td><td>two-way binds an input to a scope variable<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>ng-init<\/td><td>gives initial values to variables<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>ng-bind<\/td><td>one-way: shows a variable's value in an element<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>ng-controller<\/td><td>attaches a controller (a JS function that sets up $scope)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>ng-click<\/td><td>runs an expression or function when clicked<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;div ng-app=&quot;demo&quot; ng-controller=&quot;ctrl&quot; ng-init=&quot;count=0&quot;&gt;\n  Name: &lt;input ng-model=&quot;name&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Hello &lt;span ng-bind=&quot;name&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;button ng-click=&quot;count = count + 1&quot;&gt;Clicked {{ count }} times&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;{{ greeting }}&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  angular.module(&quot;demo&quot;, []).controller(&quot;ctrl&quot;, function ($scope) {\n    $scope.name = &quot;Ravi&quot;;\n    $scope.greeting = &quot;Set by ng-controller&quot;;\n  });\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "May24 Q21": "<p>Uses only Node's built-in <b>http<\/b>, <b>fs<\/b> and <b>querystring<\/b> modules: GET <code>/<\/code> sends payment.html; the form POSTs to <code>/payment<\/code>, where the body is collected chunk by chunk, parsed, and shown back.<\/p>\n<p><b>payment.html<\/b><\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Payment Gateway&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;form action=&quot;/payment&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;table&gt;\n      &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Card Number&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;card&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n      &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Amount&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;amount&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n      &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Account Number&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;accno&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n      &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Transfer&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;/table&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre>\n<p><b>server.js<\/b><\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const http = require(&quot;http&quot;);\nconst fs = require(&quot;fs&quot;);\nconst qs = require(&quot;querystring&quot;);\n\nhttp.createServer((req, res) =&gt; {\n  if (req.method === &quot;GET&quot; &amp;&amp; req.url === &quot;/&quot;) {\n    fs.readFile(&quot;payment.html&quot;, (err, data) =&gt; {\n      res.writeHead(200, { &quot;Content-Type&quot;: &quot;text/html&quot; });\n      res.end(data);\n    });\n  } else if (req.method === &quot;POST&quot; &amp;&amp; req.url === &quot;/payment&quot;) {\n    let body = &quot;&quot;;\n    req.on(&quot;data&quot;, (chunk) =&gt; { body += chunk; });     // collect the posted data\n    req.on(&quot;end&quot;, () =&gt; {\n      const f = qs.parse(body);                        // &quot;card=..&amp;amount=..&quot; -&gt; object\n      res.writeHead(200, { &quot;Content-Type&quot;: &quot;text/html&quot; });\n      res.end(&quot;&lt;div style=&#x27;border:1px solid black;padding:6px;width:320px&#x27;&gt;&quot; +\n              &quot;&lt;b&gt;The Transaction Details are:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&quot; +\n              &quot;Card Number: &quot; + f.card + &quot;&lt;br&gt;&quot; +\n              &quot;Amount: &quot; + f.amount + &quot;&lt;br&gt;&quot; +\n              &quot;Account Number: &quot; + f.accno + &quot;&lt;/div&gt;&quot;);\n    });\n  } else {\n    res.writeHead(404);\n    res.end(&quot;Not found&quot;);\n  }\n}).listen(2000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;Server running at http://localhost:2000/&quot;));<\/pre>\n<p><b>Run<\/b> (the form submitted with curl):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">$ node server.js\nServer running at http://localhost:2000/\n\n$ curl -X POST http://localhost:2000/payment -d &quot;card=408392323923&amp;amount=10000&amp;accno=1000230234323&quot;\n&lt;div style=&#x27;border:1px solid black;padding:6px;width:320px&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Transaction Details are:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Card Number: 408392323923&lt;br&gt;Amount: 10000&lt;br&gt;Account Number: 1000230234323&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre>\n<p>Without Express there is no body parser: the request body arrives as a stream, so <code>req.on(\"data\")<\/code> collects it and <code>req.on(\"end\")<\/code> parses it with <code>querystring.parse<\/code>.<\/p>", "May24 Q22": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    td { padding: 3px; font-size: 20px; }\n    button { width: 40px; margin: 4px; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;table&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Num1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;n1&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Num2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;n2&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Result&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;res&quot; readonly style=&quot;background:#ddd&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n  &lt;button onclick=&quot;calc(&#x27;+&#x27;)&quot;&gt;+&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button onclick=&quot;calc(&#x27;-&#x27;)&quot;&gt;-&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button onclick=&quot;calc(&#x27;*&#x27;)&quot;&gt;x&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button onclick=&quot;calc(&#x27;/&#x27;)&quot;&gt;/&lt;/button&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    function calc(op) {\n      var a = parseFloat(document.getElementById(&quot;n1&quot;).value);\n      var b = parseFloat(document.getElementById(&quot;n2&quot;).value);\n      var r;\n      if (isNaN(a) || isNaN(b)) {\n        r = &quot;Enter both numbers&quot;;\n      } else if (op == &quot;+&quot;) r = a + b;\n      else if (op == &quot;-&quot;) r = a - b;\n      else if (op == &quot;*&quot;) r = a * b;\n      else r = (b == 0) ? &quot;Cannot divide by 0&quot; : a / b;\n      document.getElementById(&quot;res&quot;).value = r;\n    }\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul><li>Each button calls the same function <code>calc()<\/code> with its operator, so the result changes on every click.<\/li>\n<li><code>parseFloat<\/code> converts the text to numbers; <code>isNaN<\/code> catches empty or non-numeric input; division by zero is handled.<\/li>\n<li>The Result box is <code>readonly<\/code> (grey, as in the picture) and is filled through its <code>value<\/code>.<\/li><\/ul>", "May24 Q23a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;#box { width: 120px; height: 60px; background: teal; color: white; padding: 8px; position: relative; margin-top: 10px; }&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;hide&quot;&gt;hide&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;show&quot;&gt;show&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;toggle&quot;&gt;toggle&lt;/button&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;fin&quot;&gt;fadeIn&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;fout&quot;&gt;fadeOut&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;fto&quot;&gt;fadeTo 0.3&lt;/button&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;sup&quot;&gt;slideUp&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;sdown&quot;&gt;slideDown&lt;/button&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;anim&quot;&gt;animate&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;div id=&quot;box&quot;&gt;Box&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    $(function () {\n      $(&quot;#hide&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).hide(500); });\n      $(&quot;#show&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).show(500); });\n      $(&quot;#toggle&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).toggle(); });\n      $(&quot;#fin&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).fadeIn(); });\n      $(&quot;#fout&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).fadeOut(); });\n      $(&quot;#fto&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).fadeTo(&quot;slow&quot;, 0.3); });\n      $(&quot;#sup&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).slideUp(); });\n      $(&quot;#sdown&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).slideDown(); });\n      $(&quot;#anim&quot;).click(function () {\n        $(&quot;#box&quot;).animate({ left: &quot;200px&quot;, width: &quot;180px&quot;, opacity: 0.6 }, 1000)\n                 .animate({ left: &quot;0px&quot;, width: &quot;120px&quot;, opacity: 1 }, 1000);\n      });\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Group<\/th><th>Methods<\/th><th>What happens<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Hide / show<\/td><td><code>hide(), show(), toggle()<\/code><\/td><td>change display; with a speed they shrink/grow<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Fading<\/td><td><code>fadeIn(), fadeOut(), fadeToggle(), fadeTo(speed, opacity)<\/code><\/td><td>change opacity gradually; fadeTo stops at a given opacity<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Sliding<\/td><td><code>slideDown(), slideUp(), slideToggle()<\/code><\/td><td>change height gradually<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Animation<\/td><td><code>animate({css}, speed)<\/code>, <code>stop()<\/code><\/td><td>animates any numeric CSS property; calls can be chained into a queue<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>All accept an optional speed (<code>\"slow\"<\/code>, <code>\"fast\"<\/code> or ms) and a callback that runs when the effect ends.<\/p>", "May24 Q23b": "<p>HTML has three kinds of list:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Ordered list<\/b> <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code>: numbered items <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code>. Attribute <code>type<\/code> = 1, A, a, I, i and <code>start<\/code> sets the first number.<\/li>\n<li><b>Unordered list<\/b> <code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code>: bulleted items; CSS <code>list-style-type<\/code> = disc, circle, square or none.<\/li>\n<li><b>Definition (description) list<\/b> <code>&lt;dl&gt;<\/code>: terms <code>&lt;dt&gt;<\/code> each followed by a description <code>&lt;dd&gt;<\/code>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h4&gt;Ordered List&lt;/h4&gt;\n  &lt;ol type=&quot;A&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;HTML&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;CSS&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;JavaScript&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ol&gt;\n\n  &lt;h4&gt;Unordered List&lt;/h4&gt;\n  &lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type: square&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Apple&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Mango&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Banana&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n\n  &lt;h4&gt;Definition List&lt;/h4&gt;\n  &lt;dl&gt;\n    &lt;dt&gt;HTML&lt;/dt&gt;\n    &lt;dd&gt;Markup language that structures a web page.&lt;/dd&gt;\n    &lt;dt&gt;CSS&lt;/dt&gt;\n    &lt;dd&gt;Style sheet language that styles the page.&lt;/dd&gt;\n  &lt;/dl&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Lists can be nested by putting a full <code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code> or <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code> inside an <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "May24 Q24": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">// i) database\nuse company\n\n// ii) collection\ndb.createCollection(&quot;employee&quot;)\n\n// iii) five employees\ndb.employee.insertMany([\n  { name: &quot;Arun&quot;, empid: 101, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, email: &quot;arun@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543210&quot;, experience: 3 },\n  { name: &quot;Bhavya&quot;, empid: 102, gender: &quot;Female&quot;, email: &quot;bhavya@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543211&quot;, experience: 5 },\n  { name: &quot;Charles&quot;, empid: 103, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, email: &quot;charles@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543212&quot;, experience: 7.5 },\n  { name: &quot;Divya&quot;, empid: 104, gender: &quot;Female&quot;, email: &quot;divya@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543213&quot;, experience: 2 },\n  { name: &quot;Elan&quot;, empid: 105, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, email: &quot;elan@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543214&quot;, experience: 4.5 }\n])\n\n// iv) search by empid\ndb.employee.find({ empid: 103 })\n\n// v) change the phone of an employee\ndb.employee.updateOne({ empid: 101 }, { $set: { phone: &quot;9000011111&quot; } })\n\n// vi) delete an employee\ndb.employee.deleteOne({ empid: 104 })\n\n// vii) experience greater than 4.5 years\ndb.employee.find({ experience: { $gt: 4.5 } }, { _id: 0, name: 1, empid: 1, experience: 1 })<\/pre>\n<p><b>Output<\/b> (run in mongosh):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">test&gt; use company\nswitched to db company\n\ncompany&gt; db.createCollection(&quot;employee&quot;)\n{ ok: 1 }\n\ncompany&gt; db.employee.insertMany([\n...   { name: &quot;Arun&quot;, empid: 101, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, email: &quot;arun@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543210&quot;, experience: 3 },\n...   { name: &quot;Bhavya&quot;, empid: 102, gender: &quot;Female&quot;, email: &quot;bhavya@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543211&quot;, experience: 5 },\n...   { name: &quot;Charles&quot;, empid: 103, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, email: &quot;charles@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543212&quot;, experience: 7.5 },\n...   { name: &quot;Divya&quot;, empid: 104, gender: &quot;Female&quot;, email: &quot;divya@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543213&quot;, experience: 2 },\n...   { name: &quot;Elan&quot;, empid: 105, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, email: &quot;elan@company.com&quot;, phone: &quot;9876543214&quot;, experience: 4.5 }\n... ])\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedIds: {\n    &#x27;0&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7b2647c709c578e842&#x27;),\n    &#x27;1&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7b2647c709c578e843&#x27;),\n    &#x27;2&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7b2647c709c578e844&#x27;),\n    &#x27;3&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7b2647c709c578e845&#x27;),\n    &#x27;4&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7b2647c709c578e846&#x27;)\n  }\n}\n\ncompany&gt; db.employee.find({ empid: 103 })\n[\n  {\n    _id: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7b2647c709c578e844&#x27;),\n    name: &#x27;Charles&#x27;,\n    empid: 103,\n    gender: &#x27;Male&#x27;,\n    email: &#x27;charles@company.com&#x27;,\n    phone: &#x27;9876543212&#x27;,\n    experience: 7.5\n  }\n]\n\ncompany&gt; db.employee.updateOne({ empid: 101 }, { $set: { phone: &quot;9000011111&quot; } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 1,\n  modifiedCount: 1,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\ncompany&gt; db.employee.deleteOne({ empid: 104 })\n{ acknowledged: true, deletedCount: 1 }\n\ncompany&gt; db.employee.find({ experience: { $gt: 4.5 } }, { _id: 0, name: 1, empid: 1, experience: 1 })\n[\n  { name: &#x27;Bhavya&#x27;, empid: 102, experience: 5 },\n  { name: &#x27;Charles&#x27;, empid: 103, experience: 7.5 }\n]<\/pre>\n<p><code>$gt<\/code> is \"greater than\", so Elan with exactly 4.5 years is <b>not<\/b> listed (use <code>$gte<\/code> to include him). Other comparison operators: <code>$lt, $lte, $eq, $ne, $in<\/code>.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q1": "<p><code>&lt;meta&gt;<\/code> gives <b>information about the page<\/b> (metadata) to the browser and search engines, not shown on the page: character set, description, keywords, author, and the viewport for mobile. E.g. <code>&lt;meta charset=\"UTF-8\"&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q2": "<p><code>$(document).ready(function(){ ... })<\/code> runs the code only <b>after the HTML (DOM) has fully loaded<\/b>, so jQuery can safely find and change the elements. Short form: <code>$(function(){ ... })<\/code>.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q3": "<p><b>String<\/b> (<code>\"Ravi\"<\/code>) and <b>Number<\/b> (<code>25<\/code>). Boolean, null, object and array are also shared by both.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q4": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<p><b>Two-way data binding<\/b>: the view and the model stay in sync automatically, so there is no need to write DOM code to update the page when data changes (or read inputs when the user types).<\/p>", "Nov24 Q5": "<p><b>var<\/b> is <b>function-scoped<\/b>, can be re-declared, and is hoisted (usable before its line, as undefined). <b>let<\/b> is <b>block-scoped<\/b> (only inside its <code>{ }<\/code>) and cannot be re-declared in the same scope. E.g. <code>if (true) { var a = 1; let b = 2; }<\/code>: <code>a<\/code> is visible after the block, <code>b<\/code> is not.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q6": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<p><b>ngRoute<\/b> is the AngularJS module for <b>routing<\/b>: it maps URLs (<code>#!/home<\/code>) to views with <code>$routeProvider<\/code> and loads them into <code>ng-view<\/code>, making a single-page application.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q7": "<p><b>&lt;img&gt;<\/b>: <code>&lt;img src=\"photo.jpg\" alt=\"photo\"&gt;<\/code><\/p>", "Nov24 Q8": "<p><code>.container<\/code> wraps the page content in a <b>responsive fixed-width box<\/b> that is centred with padding; its max-width changes at each breakpoint. (<code>.container-fluid<\/code> is always full width.) The grid's rows and columns go inside it.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q9": "<p>The <b>fs<\/b> (file system) module: <code>const fs = require(\"fs\");<\/code><\/p>", "Nov24 Q10": "<p><b>BSON<\/b> (Binary JSON): documents look like JSON but are stored in a binary form that adds types such as Date and ObjectId.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q11": "<p><code>float: left | right<\/code> takes an element <b>out of the normal flow<\/b> and pushes it to the left or right of its container; the text and inline content that follow <b>wrap around<\/b> it. Several floated blocks line up side by side (old way to build columns and nav bars). Side effects: a parent containing only floats collapses to zero height, fixed with <code>clear: both<\/code> on a following element or <code>overflow: hidden<\/code> on the parent.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;img src=&quot;https://picsum.photos/id/10/120/80&quot; style=&quot;float:left;margin-right:10px&quot; alt=&quot;img&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This text wraps around the image because the image is floated left. Floats were used for image wrapping and columns before flexbox.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=&quot;clear:both&quot;&gt;clear: both starts below the float.&lt;/p&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "Nov24 Q12": "<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>JavaScript<\/th><th>jQuery<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>A programming language built into browsers<\/td><td>A JavaScript <b>library<\/b> written in JS (must be included with a script tag)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Longer code: <code>document.getElementById(\"x\").style.display = \"none\";<\/code><\/td><td>Short, chainable code: <code>$(\"#x\").hide();<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Some cross-browser differences handled by hand<\/td><td>Handles browser differences; ready-made effects and AJAX<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>The key difference: jQuery is not a separate language; it is a library that simplifies DOM selection, events and effects that plain JavaScript does with more code.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q13": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">{\n  &quot;courseName&quot;: &quot;Web Technology&quot;,\n  &quot;courseCode&quot;: &quot;23CS2048&quot;,\n  &quot;duration&quot;: &quot;12 weeks&quot;,\n  &quot;instructor&quot;: {\n    &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Dr. Priya&quot;,\n    &quot;email&quot;: &quot;priya@karunya.edu&quot;\n  },\n  &quot;modules&quot;: [&quot;HTML &amp; CSS&quot;, &quot;JavaScript&quot;, &quot;jQuery&quot;, &quot;React&quot;, &quot;MongoDB&quot;, &quot;Node.js&quot;],\n  &quot;fee&quot;: 4999,\n  &quot;certificate&quot;: true\n}<\/pre>\n<p>Keys are in double quotes; values use JSON types: strings, a number, a boolean, a nested object (instructor) and an array (modules).<\/p>", "Nov24 Q14": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;div ng-app=&quot;&quot; ng-init=&quot;items=[{name:&#x27;Pen&#x27;,price:10},{name:&#x27;Notebook&#x27;,price:45},{name:&#x27;Bag&#x27;,price:650}]&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li ng-repeat=&quot;x in items&quot;&gt;{{ $index + 1 }}. {{ x.name }} - Rs.{{ x.price }}&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>ng-repeat=\"x in items\"<\/code> creates one <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code> per array element; <code>$index<\/code> is the position.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q15": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const http = require(&quot;http&quot;);\n\nconst server = http.createServer((req, res) =&gt; {\n  res.writeHead(200, { &quot;Content-Type&quot;: &quot;text/html&quot; });\n  res.end(&quot;&lt;h1&gt;Hello from Node.js server&lt;/h1&gt;&quot;);\n});\n\nserver.listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;Server running at http://localhost:3000/&quot;));<\/pre>\n<p><b>Run<\/b>:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">$ node server.js\nServer running at http://localhost:3000/\n\n$ curl http://localhost:3000/\n&lt;h1&gt;Hello from Node.js server&lt;/h1&gt;<\/pre>\n<p><code>createServer<\/code> takes a callback run for every request; <code>writeHead<\/code> sets the status and type, <code>end<\/code> sends the body; <code>listen<\/code> starts it on port 3000.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q16": "<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>insertOne()<\/th><th>insertMany()<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Inserts a <b>single<\/b> document<\/td><td>Inserts an <b>array<\/b> of documents in one call<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Returns <code>insertedId<\/code><\/td><td>Returns <code>insertedIds<\/code> (one per document)<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">db.students.insertOne({ name: &quot;Ravi&quot;, dept: &quot;CSE&quot; })\ndb.students.insertMany([{ name: &quot;Asha&quot;, dept: &quot;IT&quot; }, { name: &quot;John&quot;, dept: &quot;ECE&quot; }])<\/pre>\n<p>insertMany is faster for bulk data (one round trip). By default it is ordered: if one document fails (e.g. duplicate _id), the rest after it are not inserted.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q17": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Feedback&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #f4f6f9; }\n    form { width: 420px; margin: 20px auto; background: #fff; padding: 20px 24px; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px #0002; }\n    h2 { text-align: center; color: #2c5282; margin-top: 0; }\n    label { display: block; margin: 12px 0 4px; font-weight: bold; }\n    input[type=text], input[type=email], select, textarea { width: 100%; padding: 7px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 1px solid #bbb; border-radius: 4px; }\n    .inline { font-weight: normal; display: inline; margin-right: 12px; }\n    small { color: #666; }\n    .buttons { margin-top: 16px; text-align: center; }\n    button { padding: 8px 20px; margin: 0 6px; border: none; border-radius: 4px; color: #fff; background: #2c5282; cursor: pointer; }\n    button[type=reset] { background: #888; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;form action=&quot;#&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Feedback Submission&lt;/h2&gt;\n\n    &lt;label for=&quot;name&quot;&gt;Name&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;name&quot; name=&quot;name&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter your full name&quot; required&gt;\n\n    &lt;label for=&quot;email&quot;&gt;Email&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;email&quot; id=&quot;email&quot; name=&quot;email&quot; placeholder=&quot;you@example.com&quot; required&gt;\n\n    &lt;label&gt;Feedback Type&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;pos&quot; name=&quot;type&quot; value=&quot;Positive&quot; required&gt;&lt;label class=&quot;inline&quot; for=&quot;pos&quot;&gt;Positive&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;neu&quot; name=&quot;type&quot; value=&quot;Neutral&quot;&gt;&lt;label class=&quot;inline&quot; for=&quot;neu&quot;&gt;Neutral&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;neg&quot; name=&quot;type&quot; value=&quot;Negative&quot;&gt;&lt;label class=&quot;inline&quot; for=&quot;neg&quot;&gt;Negative&lt;/label&gt;\n\n    &lt;label for=&quot;cat&quot;&gt;Product Category&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;select id=&quot;cat&quot; name=&quot;category&quot; required&gt;\n      &lt;option value=&quot;&quot;&gt;-- Select a category --&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;option&gt;Electronics&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;option&gt;Clothing&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;option&gt;Books&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;option&gt;Home Appliances&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;/select&gt;\n\n    &lt;label for=&quot;comments&quot;&gt;Comments&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;textarea id=&quot;comments&quot; name=&quot;comments&quot; rows=&quot;4&quot; maxlength=&quot;250&quot;\n              placeholder=&quot;Write your feedback (max 250 characters)&quot;&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;\n    &lt;small&gt;Maximum 250 characters.&lt;/small&gt;\n\n    &lt;label class=&quot;inline&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; name=&quot;terms&quot; required&gt; I agree to the Terms and Conditions&lt;/label&gt;\n\n    &lt;div class=&quot;buttons&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;reset&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul><li>Text boxes with placeholders; <code>type=\"email\"<\/code> checks the format.<\/li>\n<li>Radio buttons share <code>name=\"type\"<\/code> so only one feedback type can be picked.<\/li>\n<li><code>&lt;select&gt;<\/code> for the category, with an empty first option so <code>required<\/code> forces a choice.<\/li>\n<li><code>&lt;textarea maxlength=\"250\"&gt;<\/code> enforces the character limit and the placeholder/small text explains it.<\/li>\n<li><code>required<\/code> on the checkbox means the form cannot be submitted until the terms are accepted.<\/li>\n<li>Submit sends the form; Reset clears it. The CSS centres the card, gives full-width fields, spacing, rounded corners and coloured buttons.<\/li><\/ul>", "Nov24 Q18a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    ul.nav {\n      list-style: none;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n      background-color: #1e4d8c;\n      display: flex;\n    }\n    ul.nav a {\n      display: block;\n      padding: 14px 22px;\n      color: white;\n      text-decoration: none;\n    }\n    ul.nav a:hover { background-color: #3a7bd5; color: #ffd54f; }\n    ul.nav a.active { background-color: #f9a825; color: #1e4d8c; font-weight: bold; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;ul class=&quot;nav&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; class=&quot;active&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Courses&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Resources&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code> structures the links; <code>list-style: none<\/code> removes bullets.<\/li>\n<li><code>display: flex<\/code> on the list lays the links out <b>horizontally<\/b>.<\/li>\n<li>Dark blue background (educational theme), <code>padding<\/code> on each link, <code>:hover<\/code> changes background and link colour.<\/li>\n<li>The <code>active<\/code> class highlights Home as the current page.<\/li><\/ul>", "Nov24 Q18b": "<ul>\n<li><b>Universal selector<\/b> <code>*<\/code>: selects <b>every<\/b> element. Used for resets: <code>* { margin: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Descendant selector<\/b> <code>A B<\/code> (a space): selects B elements anywhere <b>inside<\/b> A. <code>nav a { color: white; }<\/code> styles only links inside the nav.<\/li>\n<li><b>Pseudo-class selector<\/b> <code>:state<\/code>: selects elements in a particular <b>state or position<\/b>: <code>a:hover<\/code>, <code>input:focus<\/code>, <code>li:first-child<\/code>, <code>tr:nth-child(even)<\/code>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  * { font-family: Arial; margin: 4px; }\n  div p { color: green; }\n  li:first-child { font-weight: bold; }\n  a:hover { color: red; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Green: a p inside a div (descendant)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Not green: this p is outside the div&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;First item is bold (first-child)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Second item&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Hover turns me red&lt;/a&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "Nov24 Q19a": "<ul>\n<li><b>getElementById(id)<\/b>: finds one element; then <b>innerHTML<\/b> changes its content.<\/li>\n<li><b>createElement(tag) + appendChild(node)<\/b>: builds a new element and adds it to the page.<\/li>\n<li><b>setAttribute(name, value)<\/b> / <b>.style<\/b>: changes an attribute or style; <b>removeChild()<\/b> / <b>remove()<\/b> deletes an element.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;h3 id=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Old title&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul id=&quot;list&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;Item 1&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;img id=&quot;pic&quot; src=&quot;https://picsum.photos/id/20/80/50&quot; alt=&quot;pic&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button onclick=&quot;go()&quot;&gt;Manipulate&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  function go() {\n    document.getElementById(&quot;title&quot;).innerHTML = &quot;New title&quot;;             // change content\n    var li = document.createElement(&quot;li&quot;);                                // create\n    li.innerHTML = &quot;Item 2 (added)&quot;;\n    document.getElementById(&quot;list&quot;).appendChild(li);                      // add\n    document.getElementById(&quot;pic&quot;).setAttribute(&quot;src&quot;, &quot;https://picsum.photos/id/30/80/50&quot;);  // change attribute\n    document.getElementById(&quot;title&quot;).style.color = &quot;purple&quot;;              // change style\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "Nov24 Q19b": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;table, th, td { border: 1px solid #444; border-collapse: collapse; padding: 5px 12px; }&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h3&gt;Library Book Inventory&lt;/h3&gt;\n  &lt;table id=&quot;books&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Title&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Author&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Genre&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Price&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    var json = &#x27;{&quot;books&quot;:[&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;Title&quot;:&quot;Wings of Fire&quot;,&quot;Author&quot;:&quot;A. P. J. Abdul Kalam&quot;,&quot;Genre&quot;:&quot;Autobiography&quot;,&quot;Price&quot;:350},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;Title&quot;:&quot;The Alchemist&quot;,&quot;Author&quot;:&quot;Paulo Coelho&quot;,&quot;Genre&quot;:&quot;Fiction&quot;,&quot;Price&quot;:299},&#x27; +\n      &#x27;{&quot;Title&quot;:&quot;Clean Code&quot;,&quot;Author&quot;:&quot;Robert C. Martin&quot;,&quot;Genre&quot;:&quot;Programming&quot;,&quot;Price&quot;:899}&#x27; +\n    &#x27;]}&#x27;;\n    var lib = JSON.parse(json);\n    for (var i = 0; i &lt; lib.books.length; i++) {\n      var b = lib.books[i];\n      document.getElementById(&quot;books&quot;).innerHTML +=\n        &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + b.Title + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + b.Author + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + b.Genre + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Rs.&quot; + b.Price + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&quot;;\n    }\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The JSON text holds an array of three book objects. <code>JSON.parse()<\/code> converts it to a JavaScript object; the loop reads each book's fields and adds a table row.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q20a": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular-route.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body ng-app=&quot;spa&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!dashboard&quot;&gt;Dashboard&lt;/a&gt; |\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!profile&quot;&gt;Profile&lt;/a&gt; |\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!settings&quot;&gt;Settings&lt;/a&gt; |\n  &lt;a href=&quot;#!logout&quot;&gt;Logout&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;hr&gt;\n  &lt;div ng-view&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    angular.module(&quot;spa&quot;, [&quot;ngRoute&quot;]).config(function ($routeProvider) {\n      $routeProvider\n        .when(&quot;/dashboard&quot;, { template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;Dashboard&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome back! You have 3 new messages.&lt;/p&gt;&quot; })\n        .when(&quot;/profile&quot;,   { template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;Profile&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Name: Ananya R&lt;br&gt;Dept: CSE&lt;/p&gt;&quot; })\n        .when(&quot;/settings&quot;,  { template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;Settings&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;label&gt;&lt;input type=&#x27;checkbox&#x27;&gt; Email notifications&lt;/label&gt;&quot; })\n        .when(&quot;/logout&quot;,    { template: &quot;&lt;h3&gt;Logged out&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;You have been logged out.&lt;/p&gt;&quot; })\n        .otherwise({ redirectTo: &quot;/dashboard&quot; });\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Include <code>angular-route.js<\/code>, add <code>\"ngRoute\"<\/code> as a dependency, map each path with <code>$routeProvider.when()<\/code>, and place <code>ng-view<\/code> where the section should appear. Only that part changes on each click: a single-page application.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q20b": "<p class=\"callout\">Old syllabus (AngularJS, 20CS2056). 23CS2048 teaches React instead.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body ng-app=&quot;shop&quot; ng-controller=&quot;listCtrl&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;h3&gt;Shopping List&lt;/h3&gt;\n  &lt;form ng-submit=&quot;addItem()&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; ng-model=&quot;item&quot; placeholder=&quot;Add an item&quot; required&gt;\n    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Add&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li ng-repeat=&quot;x in items&quot;&gt;{{ x }} &lt;button ng-click=&quot;removeItem($index)&quot;&gt;x&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n  &lt;p ng-show=&quot;items.length == 0&quot;&gt;The list is empty.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    angular.module(&quot;shop&quot;, []).controller(&quot;listCtrl&quot;, function ($scope) {\n      $scope.items = [&quot;Milk&quot;, &quot;Bread&quot;];\n      $scope.addItem = function () {\n        if ($scope.item) {\n          $scope.items.push($scope.item);\n          $scope.item = &quot;&quot;;\n        }\n      };\n      $scope.removeItem = function (i) { $scope.items.splice(i, 1); };\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul><li>The <b>controller<\/b> <code>listCtrl<\/code> holds the array and the add function on <code>$scope<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>The input is bound with <code>ng-model=\"item\"<\/code>; <code>ng-submit<\/code> calls <code>addItem()<\/code>, which pushes it and clears the box.<\/li>\n<li><code>ng-repeat<\/code> redraws the list automatically whenever the array changes.<\/li><\/ul>", "Nov24 Q21": "<p><b>login.html<\/b><\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Login&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;form action=&quot;/loginResult&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;\n    Username: &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;username&quot; required&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    Password: &lt;input type=&quot;password&quot; name=&quot;password&quot; required&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Login&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre>\n<p><b>app.js<\/b><\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const express = require(&quot;express&quot;);\nconst path = require(&quot;path&quot;);\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));   // parse form data into req.body\n\napp.get(&quot;/&quot;, (req, res) =&gt; {\n  res.sendFile(path.join(__dirname, &quot;login.html&quot;));\n});\n\napp.post(&quot;/loginResult&quot;, (req, res) =&gt; {\n  const { username, password } = req.body;\n  res.send(`\n    &lt;h2&gt;Login Details&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;6&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Username&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td&gt;${username}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n      &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Password&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td&gt;${&quot;*&quot;.repeat(password.length)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;/table&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Login submitted successfully.&lt;/p&gt;`);\n});\n\napp.listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;Server running at http://localhost:3000/&quot;));<\/pre>\n<p><b>Run<\/b> (<code>npm install express<\/code>, <code>node app.js<\/code>; the form submitted with curl):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">$ node app.js\nServer running at http://localhost:3000/\n\n$ curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/loginResult -d &quot;username=ananya&amp;password=secret123&quot;\n\n    &lt;h2&gt;Login Details&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;6&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Username&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td&gt;ananya&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n      &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Password&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td&gt;*********&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;/table&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Login submitted successfully.&lt;/p&gt;<\/pre>\n<p>The form's <code>action=\"/loginResult\" method=\"post\"<\/code> sends the browser to <code>http://localhost:3000/loginResult<\/code>; <code>express.urlencoded<\/code> puts the fields in <code>req.body<\/code> and the route replies with a formatted table. The password is masked rather than echoed.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q22": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    body { font-family: Arial; }\n    .box { width: 300px; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 8px; }\n    input, select { width: 100%; padding: 6px; margin: 6px 0 12px; box-sizing: border-box; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Currency Converter&lt;/h3&gt;\n    Amount in USD:\n    &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; id=&quot;usd&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter amount in USD&quot;&gt;\n    Convert to:\n    &lt;select id=&quot;cur&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;option value=&quot;EUR&quot;&gt;EUR (Euro)&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;option value=&quot;JPY&quot;&gt;JPY (Japanese Yen)&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;/select&gt;\n    &lt;button onclick=&quot;convert()&quot;&gt;Convert&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;p id=&quot;out&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    function convert() {\n      var usd = parseFloat(document.getElementById(&quot;usd&quot;).value);\n      var cur = document.getElementById(&quot;cur&quot;).value;\n      var out = document.getElementById(&quot;out&quot;);\n      if (isNaN(usd) || usd &lt; 0) {\n        out.innerHTML = &quot;Please enter a valid amount.&quot;;\n        return;\n      }\n      var rate = (cur == &quot;EUR&quot;) ? 0.85 : 110.5;\n      var result = usd * rate;\n      out.innerHTML = usd + &quot; USD = &lt;b&gt;&quot; + result.toFixed(2) + &quot; &quot; + cur + &quot;&lt;/b&gt;&quot;;\n    }\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The amount is read with <code>parseFloat<\/code>, the rate is picked from the drop-down (EUR ×0.85, JPY ×110.5), and the result is written to the page with <code>innerHTML<\/code>, rounded with <code>toFixed(2)<\/code>. 100 USD gives 85.00 EUR or 11050.00 JPY.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q23a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;st&quot;&gt;slideToggle&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;ft&quot;&gt;fadeTo 0.4&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;anim&quot;&gt;queue 5 animations&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;stop&quot;&gt;stop&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;faq&quot; style=&quot;background:#e3f2fd;padding:10px;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;FAQ answer panel&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;ball&quot; style=&quot;width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:50%;background:tomato;position:relative&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  $(&quot;#st&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#faq&quot;).slideToggle(400); });\n  $(&quot;#ft&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#faq&quot;).fadeTo(600, 0.4); });\n  $(&quot;#anim&quot;).click(function () {\n    for (var i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) $(&quot;#ball&quot;).animate({ left: 250 }, 800).animate({ left: 0 }, 800);\n  });\n  $(&quot;#stop&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#ball&quot;).stop(true); });   // true = clear the queue too\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul>\n<li><b>slideToggle(speed)<\/b>: slides an element down if hidden and up if visible, with one button. Used for FAQ answers, dropdown menus and \"read more\" panels; the movement shows the user where content came from.<\/li>\n<li><b>fadeTo(speed, opacity)<\/b>: fades to a <b>given opacity<\/b> (e.g. 0.4) without hiding the element. Used to dim disabled items or show focus. Opacity animations are smooth on most devices, but many simultaneous or long fades can stutter on slow phones, so keep durations short (200 to 600 ms) and fade few elements at once.<\/li>\n<li><b>stop(clearQueue, jumpToEnd)<\/b>: stops the running animation. jQuery <b>queues<\/b> animations: hovering in and out quickly can pile up many, which keep playing long after. <code>stop(true)<\/code> clears the queue, so the element reacts at once and the browser does less work. Common pattern: <code>$(this).stop().slideDown()<\/code>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Together they give feedback that is smooth but not slow: content changes are visible and quick, and the page never lags behind the user.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q23b": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;ol type=&quot;I&quot; start=&quot;10&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Tomato\n      &lt;dl&gt;\n        &lt;dt&gt;Tomato:&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;A red, juicy fruit commonly used in cooking.&lt;/dd&gt;\n        &lt;dt&gt;Lycopene:&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;Tomatoes are rich in lycopene, beneficial for health.&lt;/dd&gt;\n      &lt;/dl&gt;\n    &lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Carrot\n      &lt;dl&gt;\n        &lt;dt&gt;Carrot:&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;An orange root vegetable high in beta-carotene.&lt;/dd&gt;\n        &lt;dt&gt;Vitamin A:&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;Carrots are an excellent source of Vitamin A.&lt;/dd&gt;\n      &lt;/dl&gt;\n    &lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Broccoli\n      &lt;dl&gt;\n        &lt;dt&gt;Broccoli:&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;A green vegetable rich in vitamins and minerals.&lt;/dd&gt;\n        &lt;dt&gt;Fiber:&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;Broccoli is a good source of dietary fiber.&lt;/dd&gt;\n      &lt;/dl&gt;\n    &lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The numbering X, XI, XII needs an ordered list with Roman numerals (<code>type=\"I\"<\/code>) starting at 10 (<code>start=\"10\"<\/code>). Each term with its meaning is a <b>definition list<\/b>: <code>&lt;dt&gt;<\/code> for the term and <code>&lt;dd&gt;<\/code> for the description, nested inside each <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "Nov24 Q24": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">// create / switch to the database\nuse hospital\n\n// patients collection with three patients\ndb.createCollection(&quot;patients&quot;)\n\ndb.patients.insertMany([\n  { name: &quot;Arun&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P01&quot;, age: 45, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, contact: &quot;9876500001&quot;, address: &quot;Coimbatore&quot; },\n  { name: &quot;Divya&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P02&quot;, age: 30, gender: &quot;Female&quot;, contact: &quot;9876500002&quot;, address: &quot;Chennai&quot; },\n  { name: &quot;Rahul&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P03&quot;, age: 60, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, contact: &quot;9876500003&quot;, address: &quot;Madurai&quot; }\n])\n\n// doctors collection with three doctors\ndb.createCollection(&quot;doctors&quot;)\n\ndb.doctors.insertMany([\n  { name: &quot;Dr. Meena&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot;, specialization: &quot;Cardiology&quot;, contact: &quot;9000000001&quot;, availability: &quot;Mon-Fri&quot; },\n  { name: &quot;Dr. Kumar&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D02&quot;, specialization: &quot;Neurology&quot;, contact: &quot;9000000002&quot;, availability: &quot;Tue-Sat&quot; },\n  { name: &quot;Dr. Sara&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D03&quot;, specialization: &quot;Orthopedics&quot;, contact: &quot;9000000003&quot;, availability: &quot;Mon-Wed&quot; }\n])\n\n// specialization of one doctor\ndb.doctors.find({ doctor_id: &quot;D02&quot; }, { _id: 0, name: 1, specialization: 1 })\n\n// update a patient&#x27;s contact\ndb.patients.updateOne({ patient_id: &quot;P02&quot; }, { $set: { contact: &quot;9123456789&quot; } })\n\n// assign a doctor to a patient\ndb.patients.updateOne({ patient_id: &quot;P01&quot; }, { $set: { doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot; } })\n\n// appointments collection and one appointment\ndb.createCollection(&quot;appointments&quot;)\n\ndb.appointments.insertMany([\n  { appointment_id: &quot;A01&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P01&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot;, date: new Date(&quot;2026-12-05&quot;), status: &quot;scheduled&quot; },\n  { appointment_id: &quot;A02&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P03&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot;, date: new Date(&quot;2026-12-08&quot;), status: &quot;scheduled&quot; }\n])\n\n// update an appointment&#x27;s status\ndb.appointments.updateOne({ appointment_id: &quot;A02&quot; }, { $set: { status: &quot;completed&quot; } })\n\n// upcoming appointments of a doctor\ndb.appointments.find({ doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot;, status: &quot;scheduled&quot;, date: { $gte: new Date() } })<\/pre>\n<p><b>Output<\/b> (run in mongosh):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">test&gt; use hospital\nswitched to db hospital\n\nhospital&gt; db.createCollection(&quot;patients&quot;)\n{ ok: 1 }\n\nhospital&gt; db.patients.insertMany([\n...   { name: &quot;Arun&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P01&quot;, age: 45, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, contact: &quot;9876500001&quot;, address: &quot;Coimbatore&quot; },\n...   { name: &quot;Divya&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P02&quot;, age: 30, gender: &quot;Female&quot;, contact: &quot;9876500002&quot;, address: &quot;Chennai&quot; },\n...   { name: &quot;Rahul&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P03&quot;, age: 60, gender: &quot;Male&quot;, contact: &quot;9876500003&quot;, address: &quot;Madurai&quot; }\n... ])\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedIds: {\n    &#x27;0&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7eea1b6d6df50bf869&#x27;),\n    &#x27;1&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7eea1b6d6df50bf86a&#x27;),\n    &#x27;2&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7eea1b6d6df50bf86b&#x27;)\n  }\n}\n\nhospital&gt; db.createCollection(&quot;doctors&quot;)\n{ ok: 1 }\n\nhospital&gt; db.doctors.insertMany([\n...   { name: &quot;Dr. Meena&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot;, specialization: &quot;Cardiology&quot;, contact: &quot;9000000001&quot;, availability: &quot;Mon-Fri&quot; },\n...   { name: &quot;Dr. Kumar&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D02&quot;, specialization: &quot;Neurology&quot;, contact: &quot;9000000002&quot;, availability: &quot;Tue-Sat&quot; },\n...   { name: &quot;Dr. Sara&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D03&quot;, specialization: &quot;Orthopedics&quot;, contact: &quot;9000000003&quot;, availability: &quot;Mon-Wed&quot; }\n... ])\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedIds: {\n    &#x27;0&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7f4a52505e0b870e9d&#x27;),\n    &#x27;1&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7f4a52505e0b870e9e&#x27;),\n    &#x27;2&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b7f4a52505e0b870e9f&#x27;)\n  }\n}\n\nhospital&gt; db.doctors.find({ doctor_id: &quot;D02&quot; }, { _id: 0, name: 1, specialization: 1 })\n[ { name: &#x27;Dr. Kumar&#x27;, specialization: &#x27;Neurology&#x27; } ]\n\nhospital&gt; db.patients.updateOne({ patient_id: &quot;P02&quot; }, { $set: { contact: &quot;9123456789&quot; } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 1,\n  modifiedCount: 1,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nhospital&gt; db.patients.updateOne({ patient_id: &quot;P01&quot; }, { $set: { doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot; } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 1,\n  modifiedCount: 1,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nhospital&gt; db.createCollection(&quot;appointments&quot;)\n{ ok: 1 }\n\nhospital&gt; db.appointments.insertMany([\n...   { appointment_id: &quot;A01&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P01&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot;, date: new Date(&quot;2026-12-05&quot;), status: &quot;scheduled&quot; },\n...   { appointment_id: &quot;A02&quot;, patient_id: &quot;P03&quot;, doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot;, date: new Date(&quot;2026-12-08&quot;), status: &quot;scheduled&quot; }\n... ])\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedIds: {\n    &#x27;0&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b80fe46cac19d76f075&#x27;),\n    &#x27;1&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b80fe46cac19d76f076&#x27;)\n  }\n}\n\nhospital&gt; db.appointments.updateOne({ appointment_id: &quot;A02&quot; }, { $set: { status: &quot;completed&quot; } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 1,\n  modifiedCount: 1,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nhospital&gt; db.appointments.find({ doctor_id: &quot;D01&quot;, status: &quot;scheduled&quot;, date: { $gte: new Date() } })\n[\n  {\n    _id: ObjectId(&#x27;6b022b80fe46cac19d76f075&#x27;),\n    appointment_id: &#x27;A01&#x27;,\n    patient_id: &#x27;P01&#x27;,\n    doctor_id: &#x27;D01&#x27;,\n    date: ISODate(&#x27;2026-12-05T00:00:00.000Z&#x27;),\n    status: &#x27;scheduled&#x27;\n  }\n]<\/pre>\n<ul><li>Collections are linked by ids (<code>patient_id<\/code>, <code>doctor_id<\/code>), the way foreign keys work in SQL; adding <code>doctor_id<\/code> to a patient with <code>$set<\/code> assigns the doctor.<\/li>\n<li>\"Upcoming\" means status scheduled and a date from now on: <code>{ $gte: new Date() }<\/code>. A02 was completed, so only A01 is shown.<\/li><\/ul>", "Nov25 Q1": "<p><b>&lt;img&gt;<\/b>. It is an empty tag: <code>&lt;img src=\"logo.png\" alt=\"College logo\"&gt;<\/code>. <code>src<\/code> gives the file, <code>alt<\/code> the text shown if the image cannot load.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q2": "<p>A <b>block<\/b> element starts on a new line and takes the full width (<code>&lt;div&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;p&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;h1&gt;<\/code>). An <b>inline<\/b> element stays in the line and takes only the width of its content (<code>&lt;span&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;a&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;b&gt;<\/code>).<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;p&gt;This is a block. &lt;span&gt;This span stays inline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<\/pre>", "Nov25 Q3": "<p><b>padding<\/b>, e.g. <code>padding: 10px;<\/code>. (margin is the space <i>outside<\/i> the border.)<\/p>", "Nov25 Q4": "<p><b>opacity<\/b> sets how transparent an element is, from 0 (fully transparent) to 1 (fully opaque). <code>img { opacity: 0.5; }<\/code> makes the image half see-through.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q5": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const pi = 3.14;<\/pre>", "Nov25 Q6": "<p><b>val()<\/b> gets or sets the value of a form field. <code>$(\"#name\").val()<\/code> reads what the user typed; <code>$(\"#name\").val(\"Ravi\")<\/code> sets it.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q7": "<p><b>btn btn-primary<\/b>: <code>&lt;button class=\"btn btn-primary\"&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;<\/code><\/p>", "Nov25 Q8": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"jsx\">function Greet() {\n  return &lt;p&gt;Hi there!&lt;/p&gt;;\n}<\/pre>", "Nov25 Q9": "<p>It deletes the <b>first<\/b> document in the <code>products<\/code> collection whose <code>productID<\/code> is <code>\"P101\"<\/code>. Only one document is removed even if several match; it returns <code>{ acknowledged: true, deletedCount: 1 }<\/code> (0 if none matched).<\/p>", "Nov25 Q10": "<p><b>listen()<\/b>: <code>app.listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(\"Server running on port 3000\"));<\/code> starts the Express server on port 3000.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q11": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Home&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h1&gt;Hello World!&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Learning HTML is fun!&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;img src=&quot;banner.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Homepage Banner&quot;&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>&lt;h1&gt;<\/code> gives the heading, <code>&lt;p&gt;<\/code> the paragraph and <code>&lt;img&gt;<\/code> the image, with <code>alt<\/code> shown when banner.jpg is missing (as in the preview).<\/p>", "Nov25 Q12": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  h1 {\n    color: maroon;\n    font-size: 24px;\n    background-color: beige;\n  }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;h1&gt;Styled Heading&lt;/h1&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The selector <code>h1<\/code> picks every heading; each property is written <code>property: value;<\/code> inside the braces.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q13": "<p>All three use the anchor tag <code>&lt;a&gt;<\/code>; only the <code>href<\/code> changes.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>External website<\/b>: <code>href<\/code> is a full URL. <code>target=\"_blank\"<\/code> opens it in a new tab.<\/li>\n<li><b>Email link<\/b>: <code>href=\"mailto:…\"<\/code> opens the user's mail app with the address filled in.<\/li>\n<li><b>Phone link<\/b>: <code>href=\"tel:…\"<\/code> starts a call on a phone.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.karunya.edu&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Visit Karunya&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:admin@karunya.edu&quot;&gt;Email the admin&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;tel:+919876543210&quot;&gt;Call us&lt;/a&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "Nov25 Q14": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script&gt;\n  function showMessage() {\n    alert(&quot;Submission Successful!&quot;);\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;button onclick=&quot;showMessage()&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The function is declared with <code>function<\/code>, and <code>alert()<\/code> shows the message box. Here it is called when the button is clicked.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q15": "<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>find()<\/th><th>findOne()<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Returns <b>all<\/b> documents that match the filter<\/td><td>Returns only the <b>first<\/b> matching document<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Returns a <b>cursor<\/b> (shown as an array of documents)<\/td><td>Returns a single <b>document<\/b>, or <code>null<\/code> if none match<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Used to list records<\/td><td>Used to fetch one record, e.g. by id<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">db.students.find({ dept: &quot;CSE&quot; })        // every CSE student\ndb.students.findOne({ dept: &quot;CSE&quot; })     // only the first CSE student\ndb.students.findOne({ regno: &quot;URK24CS1000&quot; })   // one student by id<\/pre>", "Nov25 Q16": "<p>Load the built-in <b>fs<\/b> (file system) module with <code>require<\/code>, then call <code>writeFile<\/code>. It creates output.txt (or overwrites it) and calls the callback when done.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const fs = require(&quot;fs&quot;);\n\nfs.writeFile(&quot;output.txt&quot;, &quot;Hello World&quot;, (err) =&gt; {\n  if (err) throw err;\n  console.log(&quot;File written successfully&quot;);\n});<\/pre>\n<p>Run it with <code>node write.js<\/code>. <code>fs.writeFileSync(\"output.txt\", \"Hello World\")<\/code> does the same job synchronously.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q17": "<p>The form groups related inputs in <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;<\/code>, ties every input to a <code>&lt;label&gt;<\/code> (accessibility), and uses HTML5 validation (<code>required<\/code>, <code>type=\"email\"<\/code>, <code>pattern<\/code>, <code>minlength<\/code>).<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Course Registration Portal&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #f2f4f8; }\n    form { width: 460px; margin: 20px auto; background: white; padding: 20px;\n           border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 8px; }\n    h2 { text-align: center; color: #1a3d7c; }\n    fieldset { border: 1px solid #ddd; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n    label { display: block; margin-top: 8px; font-weight: bold; }\n    input[type=text], input[type=email], input[type=password],\n    input[type=date], select, textarea { width: 100%; padding: 6px; box-sizing: border-box; }\n    .inline label { display: inline; font-weight: normal; margin-right: 10px; }\n    button { padding: 8px 18px; margin-top: 12px; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;form action=&quot;/register&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Course Registration Portal&lt;/h2&gt;\n\n    &lt;fieldset&gt;\n      &lt;legend&gt;Student Details&lt;/legend&gt;\n      &lt;label for=&quot;sname&quot;&gt;Student Name&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;sname&quot; name=&quot;sname&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter your full name&quot; required&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;email&quot;&gt;Email Address&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;email&quot; id=&quot;email&quot; name=&quot;email&quot; placeholder=&quot;name@example.com&quot; required&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;regno&quot;&gt;Registration Number&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;regno&quot; name=&quot;regno&quot; placeholder=&quot;e.g. URK24CS1000&quot;\n             pattern=&quot;[A-Z]{3}[0-9]{2}[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{4}&quot; required&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;pwd&quot;&gt;Password&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;password&quot; id=&quot;pwd&quot; name=&quot;pwd&quot; minlength=&quot;8&quot;\n             placeholder=&quot;At least 8 characters, with a number&quot; required&gt;\n    &lt;/fieldset&gt;\n\n    &lt;fieldset&gt;\n      &lt;legend&gt;Course Details&lt;/legend&gt;\n      &lt;label for=&quot;course&quot;&gt;Course&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;select id=&quot;course&quot; name=&quot;course&quot; required&gt;\n        &lt;option value=&quot;&quot;&gt;-- Select a course --&lt;/option&gt;\n        &lt;option&gt;Web Development&lt;/option&gt;\n        &lt;option&gt;Data Science&lt;/option&gt;\n        &lt;option&gt;Cybersecurity&lt;/option&gt;\n        &lt;option&gt;AI &amp;amp; ML&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;/select&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;start&quot;&gt;Course Start Date&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;date&quot; id=&quot;start&quot; name=&quot;start&quot; required&gt;\n\n      &lt;label&gt;Mode of Learning&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;inline&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;online&quot; name=&quot;mode&quot; value=&quot;Online&quot; required&gt;&lt;label for=&quot;online&quot;&gt;Online&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;offline&quot; name=&quot;mode&quot; value=&quot;Offline&quot;&gt;&lt;label for=&quot;offline&quot;&gt;Offline&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;hybrid&quot; name=&quot;mode&quot; value=&quot;Hybrid&quot;&gt;&lt;label for=&quot;hybrid&quot;&gt;Hybrid&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;goals&quot;&gt;Remarks / Learning Goals&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;textarea id=&quot;goals&quot; name=&quot;goals&quot; rows=&quot;3&quot; placeholder=&quot;What do you want to learn?&quot;&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;\n\n      &lt;div class=&quot;inline&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;sub&quot; name=&quot;subscribe&quot; checked&gt;\n        &lt;label for=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;Subscribe to course updates and notifications&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/fieldset&gt;\n\n    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button type=&quot;reset&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><b>How each element is used:<\/b><\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Element<\/th><th>Tag and attributes<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Text boxes<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"text\"&gt;<\/code> and <code>type=\"email\"<\/code> (the browser checks the @ format); <code>pattern<\/code> checks the register number format<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Password<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"password\" minlength=\"8\"&gt;<\/code>, characters are hidden<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Date selector<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"date\"&gt;<\/code> shows a calendar picker<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Text area<\/td><td><code>&lt;textarea rows=\"3\"&gt;<\/code> for multi-line remarks<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Check box<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"checkbox\"&gt;<\/code>, can be ticked on or off<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Radio buttons<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"radio\"&gt;<\/code> with the <b>same name<\/b>, so only one can be chosen<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Dropdown<\/td><td><code>&lt;select&gt;<\/code> with <code>&lt;option&gt;<\/code>s; the empty first option plus <code>required<\/code> forces a choice<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Buttons<\/td><td><code>type=\"submit\"<\/code> sends the form to <code>action<\/code> by <code>method<\/code>; <code>type=\"reset\"<\/code> clears it<\/td><\/tr>\n<\/table>\n<p><code>required<\/code> stops submission while a field is empty; <code>&lt;label for&gt;<\/code> lets a screen reader (and a click) find each field; <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;<\/code> and <code>&lt;legend&gt;<\/code> give the semantic grouping.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q18a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Seminar Timetable&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; }\n    th, td { padding: 8px 14px; text-align: center; }\n    th { background-color: #d9e2f3; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;table&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;th colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Seminar Timetable&lt;/th&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Day 1&lt;/th&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Day 2&lt;/th&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Welcome Address (9:00 - 9:30 AM)&lt;/td&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Web Technologies&lt;br&gt;9:30 - 11:00 AM&lt;br&gt;Dr. Ravi Kumar&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Cloud Computing&lt;br&gt;9:30 - 11:00 AM&lt;br&gt;Dr. Anitha S&lt;/td&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Artificial Intelligence&lt;br&gt;11:30 AM - 1:00 PM&lt;br&gt;Prof. John Paul&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Cyber Security&lt;br&gt;11:30 AM - 1:00 PM&lt;br&gt;Prof. Meena R&lt;/td&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Borders<\/b>: <code>border<\/code> on table, th and td; <code>border-collapse: collapse<\/code> merges double lines into one.<\/li>\n<li><b>Header row<\/b>: <code>&lt;th colspan=\"2\"&gt;<\/code> makes \"Seminar Timetable\" span both columns.<\/li>\n<li><b>Day labels<\/b>: second row of <code>&lt;th&gt;<\/code> cells.<\/li>\n<li><b>Merged session<\/b>: <code>&lt;td colspan=\"2\"&gt;<\/code> for \"Welcome Address\".<\/li>\n<li><b>Rows 4 and 5<\/b>: one session per day, each cell giving the session name, time and speaker.<\/li>\n<li><code>rowspan<\/code> merges cells vertically, e.g. <code>&lt;td rowspan=\"2\"&gt;Lunch&lt;/td&gt;<\/code> would cover two rows of one column. This layout only needs colspan.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Nov25 Q18b": "<p>The <code>position<\/code> property decides how an element is placed. The default is <code>static<\/code> (normal flow).<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Relative<\/b>: the element stays in the normal flow (its space is kept), but is shifted from <b>where it would normally be<\/b> by top/left/right/bottom.<\/li>\n<li><b>Absolute<\/b>: the element is taken <b>out<\/b> of the normal flow (other elements close the gap) and placed relative to its <b>nearest positioned ancestor<\/b> (one with position other than static), or the page if there is none.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Applied to the timetable: the table is made <code>relative<\/code> and moved 20px right and 10px down; a \"NEW\" badge is placed with <code>absolute<\/code> at the table's top-right corner. Because the table is positioned, the badge is measured from the table, not from the page.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; }\n    th, td { padding: 8px 14px; text-align: center; }\n\n    /* (i) relative: moved from its normal place, space still reserved */\n    .timetable {\n      position: relative;\n      top: 10px;\n      left: 20px;\n    }\n\n    /* (ii) absolute: placed inside the nearest positioned ancestor (the table) */\n    .badge {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: -12px;\n      right: -12px;\n      background: red;\n      color: white;\n      padding: 3px 8px;\n      border-radius: 10px;\n      font-size: 12px;\n    }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;table class=&quot;timetable&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Seminar Timetable &lt;span class=&quot;badge&quot;&gt;NEW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Day 1&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Day 2&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Welcome Address&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Web Technologies&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Cloud Computing&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Artificial Intelligence&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Cyber Security&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th><\/th><th>Relative<\/th><th>Absolute<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>In normal flow?<\/td><td>Yes, its space is kept<\/td><td>No, removed from flow<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Offsets measured from<\/td><td>its own normal position<\/td><td>nearest positioned ancestor<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Typical use<\/td><td>small nudges; acting as the container for absolute children<\/td><td>badges, tooltips, overlays<\/td><\/tr><\/table>", "Nov25 Q19a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    .card {\n      width: 300px;\n      padding: 15px;\n      margin: 20px;\n      border: 2px solid #1a3d7c;\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      background-color: #ffffff;\n      transition: background-color 0.5s ease;\n    }\n    .card:hover {\n      background-color: #dbe9ff;\n    }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;card&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Student Information&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Name:&lt;/b&gt; Ananya R&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reg No:&lt;/b&gt; URK24CS1000&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Department:&lt;/b&gt; CSE&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>width: 300px<\/code>, <code>padding: 15px<\/code> (inside the border), <code>margin: 20px<\/code> (outside the border) and <code>border: 2px solid<\/code> follow the box model: content → padding → border → margin.<\/li>\n<li><code>:hover<\/code> applies the new background when the mouse is over the card.<\/li>\n<li><code>transition: background-color 0.5s ease<\/code> makes the colour change smoothly over half a second instead of instantly. Hover over the preview to see it.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Nov25 Q19b": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Travel World&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Popular Travel Destinations&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Paris\n      &lt;ol&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Eiffel Tower&lt;/li&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Louvre Museum&lt;/li&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Notre-Dame&lt;/li&gt;\n      &lt;/ol&gt;\n    &lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Tokyo&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Dubai&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code> gives a bulleted (unordered) list, since the destinations have no order. The attractions are ranked, so they use <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code> (numbered). The nested <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code> must sit <b>inside<\/b> Paris's <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code>, before its closing tag, not directly inside the <code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q20": "<p>Kilogram = Grams / 1000.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Grams to Kilograms&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }\n    .box { width: 320px; margin: 20px auto; padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 8px; }\n    input { width: 100%; padding: 6px; box-sizing: border-box; }\n    button { margin-top: 10px; padding: 6px 14px; }\n    #result { margin-top: 12px; font-weight: bold; }\n    .error { color: red; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Weight Converter&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;form id=&quot;convForm&quot; onsubmit=&quot;return false;&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;label for=&quot;grams&quot;&gt;Weight in grams&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;grams&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter weight in grams&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; onclick=&quot;convert()&quot;&gt;Convert&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;reset&quot; onclick=&quot;clearResult()&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n    &lt;div id=&quot;result&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    function convert() {\n      var g = document.getElementById(&quot;grams&quot;).value.trim();\n      var out = document.getElementById(&quot;result&quot;);\n\n      if (g === &quot;&quot; || isNaN(g)) {\n        out.className = &quot;error&quot;;\n        out.innerHTML = &quot;Please enter a valid number.&quot;;\n        return;\n      }\n      if (Number(g) &lt; 0) {\n        out.className = &quot;error&quot;;\n        out.innerHTML = &quot;Weight cannot be negative.&quot;;\n        return;\n      }\n      var kg = Number(g) / 1000;\n      out.className = &quot;&quot;;\n      out.innerHTML = g + &quot; g = &quot; + kg + &quot; kg&quot;;\n    }\n\n    function clearResult() {\n      document.getElementById(&quot;result&quot;).innerHTML = &quot;&quot;;\n    }\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Text box<\/b> with the required placeholder; <b>Convert<\/b> calls <code>convert()<\/code>; <b>Reset<\/b> (<code>type=\"reset\"<\/code>) clears the box, and <code>clearResult()<\/code> clears the output.<\/li>\n<li><b>Validation<\/b>: empty input, non-numbers (<code>isNaN<\/code>) and negative values show a red error instead of a result.<\/li>\n<li><b>Dynamic output<\/b>: <code>innerHTML<\/code> of the result div is updated without reloading the page. Try 2500 in the preview, which gives 2.5 kg.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Nov25 Q21": "<p>The images start hidden with <code>display:none<\/code>, and each button calls one jQuery effect.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Product Showcase&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    .product { display: inline-block; width: 150px; margin: 10px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top; }\n    .product img { width: 140px; height: 100px; display: none; }\n    .desc { display: none; font-size: 13px; background: #eef; padding: 5px; }\n    button { margin: 3px; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Product Showcase&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;show&quot;&gt;Show&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;hide&quot;&gt;Hide&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;fadein&quot;&gt;Fade In&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;fadeout&quot;&gt;Fade Out&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;slidedown&quot;&gt;Slide Down&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;slideup&quot;&gt;Slide Up&lt;/button&gt;\n\n  &lt;div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;product&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;img src=&quot;https://picsum.photos/id/0/140/100&quot; alt=&quot;Laptop&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;desc&quot;&gt;Laptop - 16 GB RAM, 512 GB SSD&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;product&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;img src=&quot;https://picsum.photos/id/250/140/100&quot; alt=&quot;Camera&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;desc&quot;&gt;Camera - 24 MP, 4K video&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;product&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;img src=&quot;https://picsum.photos/id/96/140/100&quot; alt=&quot;Headphones&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;desc&quot;&gt;Headphones - wireless, noise cancelling&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    $(document).ready(function () {\n      $(&quot;#show&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.product img&quot;).show(); });\n      $(&quot;#hide&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.product img&quot;).hide(); });\n      $(&quot;#fadein&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.product img&quot;).fadeIn(1000); });\n      $(&quot;#fadeout&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.product img&quot;).fadeOut(1000); });\n      $(&quot;#slidedown&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.desc&quot;).slideDown(); });\n      $(&quot;#slideup&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.desc&quot;).slideUp(); });\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>What it does<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>show()<\/code> / <code>hide()<\/code><\/td><td>display or hide instantly (sets display)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>fadeIn(ms)<\/code> / <code>fadeOut(ms)<\/code><\/td><td>change opacity gradually over the given time, then show / hide<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>slideDown()<\/code> / <code>slideUp()<\/code><\/td><td>animate the height to reveal / hide, like a drawer<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><code>$(document).ready()<\/code> waits until the page has loaded before attaching the click handlers; <code>$(\".product img\")<\/code> selects all three images at once.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q22": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">// 1. object\nlet smartDevice = {\n  deviceName: &quot;Smartwatch X100&quot;,\n  deviceId: 102,\n  category: &quot;Wearables&quot;,\n  specs: [&quot;Heart Rate Monitor&quot;, &quot;GPS&quot;, &quot;Water Resistant&quot;],\n  available: false,\n  price: 14999.99\n};\n\n// 2. serialization: object -&gt; JSON string\nlet jsonStr = JSON.stringify(smartDevice);\nconsole.log(&quot;Serialized JSON:&quot;);\nconsole.log(jsonStr);\n\n// 3. deserialization: JSON string -&gt; object\nlet device = JSON.parse(jsonStr);\nconsole.log(&quot;Deserialized object:&quot;);\nconsole.log(device);\n\n// 4. read values from the object\nconsole.log(&quot;Device ID: &quot; + device.deviceId);\nconsole.log(&quot;Second spec: &quot; + device.specs[1]);\n\nif (device.price &gt; 10000) {\n  console.log(&quot;Over Priced&quot;);\n} else {\n  console.log(&quot;Normal Price&quot;);\n}<\/pre>\n<p><b>Output<\/b> (run with node):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">Serialized JSON:\n{&quot;deviceName&quot;:&quot;Smartwatch X100&quot;,&quot;deviceId&quot;:102,&quot;category&quot;:&quot;Wearables&quot;,&quot;specs&quot;:[&quot;Heart Rate Monitor&quot;,&quot;GPS&quot;,&quot;Water Resistant&quot;],&quot;available&quot;:false,&quot;price&quot;:14999.99}\nDeserialized object:\n{\n  deviceName: &#x27;Smartwatch X100&#x27;,\n  deviceId: 102,\n  category: &#x27;Wearables&#x27;,\n  specs: [ &#x27;Heart Rate Monitor&#x27;, &#x27;GPS&#x27;, &#x27;Water Resistant&#x27; ],\n  available: false,\n  price: 14999.99\n}\nDevice ID: 102\nSecond spec: GPS\nOver Priced<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Serialization<\/b>: <code>JSON.stringify()<\/code> turns the object into a string, so it can be stored or sent. Keys get double quotes.<\/li>\n<li><b>Deserialization<\/b>: <code>JSON.parse()<\/code> turns the string back into an object whose properties can be used.<\/li>\n<li>Arrays are zero-indexed, so the second spec is <code>specs[1]<\/code> = \"GPS\". 14999.99 &gt; 10000, so it prints \"Over Priced\".<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>To show it on the web page instead of the console, write each line with <code>document.getElementById(\"out\").innerHTML += …<\/code>.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q23": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">// i) create / switch to the database\nuse hospitalDB\n\n// ii) create the collection\ndb.createCollection(&quot;patients&quot;)\n\n// iii) insert 3 patients\ndb.patients.insertMany([\n  { patientID: &quot;P001&quot;, name: &quot;Arun Kumar&quot;, age: 45, department: &quot;Cardiology&quot;,\n    admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-11-02&quot;), dischargeDate: null, status: &quot;admitted&quot; },\n  { patientID: &quot;P002&quot;, name: &quot;Divya S&quot;, age: 32, department: &quot;Neurology&quot;,\n    admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-10-20&quot;), dischargeDate: new Date(&quot;2025-10-28&quot;), status: &quot;discharged&quot; },\n  { patientID: &quot;P003&quot;, name: &quot;Rahul M&quot;, age: 60, department: &quot;Orthopedics&quot;,\n    admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-11-05&quot;), dischargeDate: null, status: &quot;under observation&quot; }\n])\n\n// iv) one patient by patientID\ndb.patients.findOne({ patientID: &quot;P002&quot; })\n\n// v) delete a patient by patientID\ndb.patients.deleteOne({ patientID: &quot;P002&quot; })\n\n// vi) all Cardiology patients\ndb.patients.find({ department: &quot;Cardiology&quot; })\n\n// vii) add insuranceProvider to every patient\ndb.patients.updateMany({}, { $set: { insuranceProvider: &quot;Not Provided&quot; } })\n\n// viii) update a patient&#x27;s status\ndb.patients.updateOne({ patientID: &quot;P003&quot; }, { $set: { status: &quot;admitted&quot; } })\n\n// ix) name, department, status sorted by admissionDate (newest first)\ndb.patients.find({}, { name: 1, department: 1, status: 1, _id: 0 }).sort({ admissionDate: -1 })\n\n// x) count patients currently admitted\ndb.patients.countDocuments({ status: &quot;admitted&quot; })<\/pre>\n<p><b>Output<\/b> (run in mongosh):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">test&gt; use hospitalDB\nswitched to db hospitalDB\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.createCollection(&quot;patients&quot;)\n{ ok: 1 }\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.insertMany([\n...   { patientID: &quot;P001&quot;, name: &quot;Arun Kumar&quot;, age: 45, department: &quot;Cardiology&quot;,\n...     admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-11-02&quot;), dischargeDate: null, status: &quot;admitted&quot; },\n...   { patientID: &quot;P002&quot;, name: &quot;Divya S&quot;, age: 32, department: &quot;Neurology&quot;,\n...     admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-10-20&quot;), dischargeDate: new Date(&quot;2025-10-28&quot;), status: &quot;discharged&quot; },\n...   { patientID: &quot;P003&quot;, name: &quot;Rahul M&quot;, age: 60, department: &quot;Orthopedics&quot;,\n...     admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-11-05&quot;), dischargeDate: null, status: &quot;under observation&quot; }\n... ])\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedIds: {\n    &#x27;0&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5b&#x27;),\n    &#x27;1&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5c&#x27;),\n    &#x27;2&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5d&#x27;)\n  }\n}\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.findOne({ patientID: &quot;P002&quot; })\n{\n  _id: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5c&#x27;),\n  patientID: &#x27;P002&#x27;,\n  name: &#x27;Divya S&#x27;,\n  age: 32,\n  department: &#x27;Neurology&#x27;,\n  admissionDate: ISODate(&#x27;2025-10-20T00:00:00.000Z&#x27;),\n  dischargeDate: ISODate(&#x27;2025-10-28T00:00:00.000Z&#x27;),\n  status: &#x27;discharged&#x27;\n}\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.deleteOne({ patientID: &quot;P002&quot; })\n{ acknowledged: true, deletedCount: 1 }\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.find({ department: &quot;Cardiology&quot; })\n[\n  {\n    _id: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5b&#x27;),\n    patientID: &#x27;P001&#x27;,\n    name: &#x27;Arun Kumar&#x27;,\n    age: 45,\n    department: &#x27;Cardiology&#x27;,\n    admissionDate: ISODate(&#x27;2025-11-02T00:00:00.000Z&#x27;),\n    dischargeDate: null,\n    status: &#x27;admitted&#x27;\n  }\n]\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.updateMany({}, { $set: { insuranceProvider: &quot;Not Provided&quot; } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 2,\n  modifiedCount: 2,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.updateOne({ patientID: &quot;P003&quot; }, { $set: { status: &quot;admitted&quot; } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 1,\n  modifiedCount: 1,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.find({}, { name: 1, department: 1, status: 1, _id: 0 }).sort({ admissionDate: -1 })\n[\n  { name: &#x27;Rahul M&#x27;, department: &#x27;Orthopedics&#x27;, status: &#x27;admitted&#x27; },\n  { name: &#x27;Arun Kumar&#x27;, department: &#x27;Cardiology&#x27;, status: &#x27;admitted&#x27; }\n]\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.countDocuments({ status: &quot;admitted&quot; })\n2<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li><code>use<\/code> creates the database the moment something is stored in it; <code>createCollection<\/code> creates the collection explicitly (an insert would also create it).<\/li>\n<li><code>updateMany({}, …)<\/code>: the empty filter <code>{}<\/code> matches every document; <code>$set<\/code> adds the field or changes it.<\/li>\n<li>Projection <code>{ name: 1, department: 1, status: 1, _id: 0 }<\/code> shows only those fields; <code>sort({ admissionDate: -1 })<\/code> is descending.<\/li>\n<li>(v) removed the discharged patient P002 and (viii) moved P003 from \"under observation\" to \"admitted\", so (x) counts 2.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Nov25 Q24": "<p>Express handles the routes; <b>Mongoose<\/b> connects to MongoDB and defines the Student model. Setup: <code>npm init -y<\/code>, then <code>npm install express mongoose<\/code>, start MongoDB, run <code>node server.js<\/code>.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">// server.js\nconst express = require(&quot;express&quot;);\nconst mongoose = require(&quot;mongoose&quot;);\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use(express.json());          // read JSON request bodies\n\n// connect to MongoDB\nmongoose.connect(&quot;mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/universityDB&quot;)\n  .then(() =&gt; console.log(&quot;Connected to MongoDB&quot;))\n  .catch((err) =&gt; console.log(&quot;DB connection error:&quot;, err.message));\n\n// schema and model\nconst studentSchema = new mongoose.Schema({\n  name: { type: String, required: true, unique: true, trim: true },\n  department: { type: String, required: true },\n  cgpa: { type: Number, required: true, min: 0, max: 10 }\n});\nconst Student = mongoose.model(&quot;Student&quot;, studentSchema);\n\n// POST /api/addStudent : add a new student\napp.post(&quot;/api/addStudent&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; {\n  try {\n    const { name, department, cgpa } = req.body;\n    if (!name || !department || cgpa === undefined) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ message: &quot;name, department and cgpa are required&quot; });\n    }\n    const existing = await Student.findOne({ name: name.trim() });\n    if (existing) {\n      return res.status(409).json({ message: &quot;Student with this name already exists&quot; });\n    }\n    const student = new Student({ name, department, cgpa });\n    await student.save();\n    res.status(201).json({ message: &quot;Student added successfully&quot;, student });\n  } catch (err) {\n    if (err.code === 11000) {               // unique index caught a duplicate\n      return res.status(409).json({ message: &quot;Student with this name already exists&quot; });\n    }\n    if (err.name === &quot;ValidationError&quot;) {   // schema rule broken, e.g. cgpa &gt; 10\n      return res.status(400).json({ message: err.message });\n    }\n    res.status(500).json({ message: &quot;Error adding student&quot;, error: err.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// GET /api/viewAllStudents : fetch all students\napp.get(&quot;/api/viewAllStudents&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; {\n  try {\n    const students = await Student.find();\n    res.status(200).json(students);\n  } catch (err) {\n    res.status(500).json({ message: &quot;Error fetching students&quot;, error: err.message });\n  }\n});\n\napp.listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;Server running on http://localhost:3000&quot;));<\/pre>\n<p><b>Testing it<\/b> (Postman, or curl as below), with the real responses:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">$ node server.js\nServer running on http://localhost:3000\nConnected to MongoDB\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ananya R&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;CSE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:8.7}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Student added successfully&quot;,&quot;student&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ananya R&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;CSE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:8.7,&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6b0205545b35f6c592f385d1&quot;,&quot;__v&quot;:0}}\n(HTTP 201)\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Karthik S&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;ECE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:7.9}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Student added successfully&quot;,&quot;student&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Karthik S&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;ECE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:7.9,&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6b0205545b35f6c592f385d2&quot;,&quot;__v&quot;:0}}\n(HTTP 201)\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ananya R&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;IT&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:9.1}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Student with this name already exists&quot;}\n(HTTP 409)\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Meera&quot;}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;name, department and cgpa are required&quot;}\n(HTTP 400)\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Meera&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;EEE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:12}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Student validation failed: cgpa: Path `cgpa` (12) is more than maximum allowed value (10).&quot;}\n(HTTP 400)\n\n$ curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/viewAllStudents\n[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6b0205545b35f6c592f385d1&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ananya R&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;CSE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:8.7,&quot;__v&quot;:0},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6b0205545b35f6c592f385d2&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Karthik S&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;ECE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:7.9,&quot;__v&quot;:0}]\n(HTTP 200)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Duplicate check<\/b>: before saving, <code>findOne({ name })<\/code> looks for the same name and returns <b>409 Conflict<\/b> with a message. <code>unique: true<\/code> in the schema is a second guard at the database level: if two requests race past the check, MongoDB rejects the second with error code 11000, which the catch also turns into 409.<\/li>\n<li><b>Validation<\/b>: missing fields give <b>400 Bad Request<\/b>; the schema enforces types and 0 ≤ CGPA ≤ 10, and a broken rule (a <code>ValidationError<\/code>) is also returned as 400, as the CGPA 12 request shows.<\/li>\n<li><b>Error handling<\/b>: each route is wrapped in <code>try/catch<\/code>; anything else (e.g. the database is down) returns <b>500<\/b> with the error message.<\/li>\n<li>Status codes: 201 Created for a new student, 200 OK for the list.<\/li>\n<\/ul>"};
